{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:56:16", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8080ccf8-5463-42f2-b01e-e1d486d448c4', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Fix UI readability issue on the recovery page where black text on dark background makes content nearly impossible to read. This is Milestone 1: Analysis and Architecture phase - need to understand current RecoveryDashboard implementation and identify specific CSS/styling issues causing readability problems. Focus on analysis and documentation rather than implementing fixes.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "task_files": [\n    "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md",\n    "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md",\n    "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n  ]\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Qi6ZWdiNdJYakvRdBa1bPV', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Qi6ZWdiNdJYakvRdBa1bPV', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/whimsical-names-utility", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "rc/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/output/brass_band_achievements_requirements.md", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/whimsical-agent-names/"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "15dc55cd7e0cba90ab4cc7319c6899ef53c2625a", "message": "V1 Cleanup: Fix bugs, remove unused code, harden security", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "11 minutes ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "15dc55cd7e0cba90ab4cc7319c6899ef53c2625a", "message": "V1 Cleanup: Fix bugs, remove unused code, harden security", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "11 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "084a9e8f01f2a2a09a54d4047dbc9b9ac6db9bc9", "message": "Complete Achievement System Expansion milestone 1: foundation planning, architecture, and task breakdown for 100 DCI and NABBA themed achievements", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "49 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "45b57283cde635a516d868d6bef8c96660a2376d", "message": "Complete milestone 1 planning: Whimsical Name Generator foundation architecture and task breakdown", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "49 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "8d043ba9766733f56edb126e12ec12a5db158e6e", "message": "Add comprehensive agent hierarchy documentation and spawn permissions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "77 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "784833714132d5a2d9def39d867f3446186ee901", "message": "Add Best Practices and Anti-Patterns to all agent definitions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "80 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M4k7jvF5X7ikNipFnVjF4A', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M4k7jvF5X7ikNipFnVjF4A', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Fix the unreadable text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) where black text appears on dark backgrounds, making it nearly impossible to read.\\n\\n**Problem**: Users report that the Improve page has severe readability issues with black text on dark backgrounds, creating a poor user experience and making the interface unusable in some areas.\\n\\n**Solution**: Identify and fix all instances of poor contrast between text and background colors to ensure proper readability across all UI elements.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Core Requirements\\n1. **Readability Fix**: Ensure all text on the Improve page is readable with proper contrast\\n2. **Bootstrap Consistency**: Maintain Bootstrap theme consistency while fixing contrast issues\\n3. **Dark Mode Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work properly in both light and dark mode contexts\\n4. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG guidelines for text contrast (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text)\\n\\n### Specific Issues to Address\\n1. **Card Backgrounds**: Review all Card components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` and ensure text is white/light\\n2. **Alert Styling**: Ensure Alert components have proper text contrast\\n3. **Badge Colors**: Verify Badge components maintain readability\\n4. **Auto-Apply Toggle**: Check styling of the toggle switch and associated text\\n5. **Table Content**: Ensure table text is readable against backgrounds\\n6. **Modal Content**: Verify modal text readability\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Cannot break existing functionality\\n- Must preserve current color scheme intent (danger/warning/success indicators)\\n- Should use Bootstrap\'s built-in text color classes where possible\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page is readable with adequate contrast\\n2. No functionality is broken by the styling changes\\n3. Design maintains visual hierarchy and color-coded meanings\\n4. Changes are minimal and focused on contrast fixes only\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to other pages\\n- Functionality modifications\\n- Theme system overhaul\\n\\n## Analysis of Current Issues\\nBased on the SelfImprovementDashboard code review, potential problem areas:\\n\\n1. **Lines 266-267**: `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` - This should be correct\\n2. **Lines 433-434**: Card with conditional background (`bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}`) - Light background with dark text should be readable\\n3. **Lines 451**: `bg-dark` class usage in auto-apply warning section\\n\\nThe issue might be in CSS overrides or Bootstrap theme customization that\'s causing text to appear black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes being used.\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- User is referring to the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page)\\n- Issue is with CSS/styling, not functional behavior\\n- Bootstrap framework is being used correctly in most places\\n- Problem may be in CSS overrides or theme customization\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n1. Analyze current styling and identify specific contrast violations\\n2. Fix styling issues using appropriate Bootstrap classes or custom CSS\\n3. Test readability across different states (auto-apply on/off, different card states)\\n4. Ensure accessibility compliance\\n5. Verify no regressions in functionality or other visual elements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SDQZusS9YdzWk2S16XpzbD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SDQZusS9YdzWk2S16XpzbD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: British Brass Band Achievements\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis project extends the existing Ensemble achievements system by adding a new \\"BRASS_BAND\\" achievement category. This follows an **extension pattern** - adding new content to an existing, well-structured system without modifying core architecture.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Plugin/Extension pattern for achievement categories\\n**Approach Rationale**: The existing achievements system is well-designed with clear enum-based categories and a list-based achievement registry. We simply extend these existing structures.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Stack (Maintained)\\n- **Backend**: Python with typed dataclasses for Achievement models\\n- **Frontend**: React with Bootstrap for UI components\\n- **State Management**: Props-based filtering in React components\\n- **API**: Existing achievement endpoints (no changes needed)\\n\\n### No New Dependencies Required\\nThe existing stack fully supports this extension.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n**1. AchievementCategory Enum** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Has SKA and other categories\\n- **Change**: Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` enum value\\n\\n**2. ACHIEVEMENTS List** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Contains Achievement objects for existing categories\\n- **Change**: Add 15 new Achievement objects for BRASS_BAND category\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n**3. AchievementsDashboard** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`)\\n- **Filter Dropdown**: Add brass_band option with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n- **getCategoryBadge Function**: Handle brass_band category styling\\n- **Fun Facts Section**: Optionally add brass band trivia\\n\\n### Component Interaction Flow\\n```\\nUser selects \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n    \\u2193\\nAchievementsDashboard filters by category=\\"brass_band\\"\\n    \\u2193\\nAPI returns achievements with category BRASS_BAND\\n    \\u2193\\nUI displays brass band achievements with proper badges\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py          # MODIFY: Add enum + 15 achievements\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # MODIFY: Add filter + badge\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Object (Existing Pattern)\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,  # NEW CATEGORY\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Achievement Definitions (15 Total)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Trigger Type |\\n|----|------|--------|--------|--------------|\\n| championship_section | Championship Section | LEGENDARY | 200 | total_executions >= 50 |\\n| silver_band | Silver Band | RARE | 50 | consecutive_successes >= 5 |\\n| principal_cornet | Principal Cornet | UNCOMMON | 30 | sub_agents_led >= 3 |\\n| adjudicator | The Adjudicator | RARE | 60 | test_evaluations >= 25 |\\n| test_piece | Test Piece Mastery | UNCOMMON | 25 | iterations_in_task > 10 |\\n| bandroom_practice | Bandroom Practice | COMMON | 15 | total_executions >= 10 |\\n| promotion | Section Promotion | EPIC | 100 | success_rate_improvement |\\n| brass_section_harmony | Brass Section Harmony | RARE | 45 | concurrent_completions |\\n| march_on_stage | March on Stage | COMMON | 10 | first_task_in_project |\\n| quick_march | Quick March | RARE | 40 | task_time < 10s |\\n| hymn_tune_encore | Hymn Tune Encore | UNCOMMON | 35 | recovery_from_failure |\\n| grand_shield | Grand Shield | EPIC | 120 | consecutive_successes >= 25 |\\n| fanfare | Fanfare | RARE | 55 | achievements_in_session >= 5 |\\n| youth_band_graduate | Youth Band Graduate | UNCOMMON | 20 | new_agent_first_10_tasks |\\n| national_finals | National Finals | LEGENDARY | 150 | project_completion |\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API Changes Required**\\n- Existing `/api/achievements` endpoint supports category filtering\\n- Frontend already handles dynamic category data\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Testing\\n1. Verify BRASS_BAND enum exists\\n2. Verify 15 achievements load without errors\\n3. Verify achievement triggering works\\n4. Run existing achievement test suite\\n\\n### Frontend Testing\\n1. Verify brass_band filter appears in dropdown\\n2. Verify filter functionality works\\n3. Verify badge displays correctly\\n4. Verify no console errors\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n- Load AchievementsDashboard\\n- Select \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n- Verify achievements display with correct icons/badges\\n- Verify at least one achievement can trigger\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend (achievements.py)\\n1. Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to AchievementCategory enum\\n2. Add 15 Achievement objects to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. Verify file imports correctly\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend (AchievementsDashboard.jsx)\\n1. Add brass_band to category filter dropdown\\n2. Update getCategoryBadge function\\n3. Optionally add fun facts\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Integration Testing\\n1. Run existing tests\\n2. Manual verification\\n3. Commit changes\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Condition Compatibility\\n**Impact**: New trigger conditions might not work with existing tracker\\n**Mitigation**: Use only existing trigger condition types\\n\\n### Risk 2: Frontend Filter Inconsistency\\n**Impact**: Filter might not match backend category name\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure exact string match \\"brass_band\\"\\n\\n## Key Implementation Decisions\\n\\n1. **Enum Value**: Use `brass_band` (lowercase with underscore) matching existing pattern\\n2. **Icon**: Use \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary icon since cornet emoji unavailable\\n3. **Trigger Conditions**: Reuse existing types, no new event tracking\\n4. **Points Range**: Follow existing scale based on rarity\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. \\u2705 BRASS_BAND in AchievementCategory enum\\n2. \\u2705 15 achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. \\u2705 brass_band filter works in UI\\n4. \\u2705 getCategoryBadge handles brass_band\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 No console errors in frontend\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KNiuEWKiY2rh9m8Hgz1LV5', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KNiuEWKiY2rh9m8Hgz1LV5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks - Milestone 1: Analysis and Investigation\\n\\n## Overview\\nIdentify all readability issues and their root causes in the SelfImprovementDashboard component where text appears black on dark backgrounds, making it unreadable.\\n\\n## User Flow: Investigation and Analysis\\nThis milestone focuses on systematic analysis to understand the scope and root causes of the readability problems before implementing fixes.\\n\\n## Task Breakdown\\n\\n### Task 1: Component Structure Analysis\\n**Task Name**: Analyze SelfImprovementDashboard component structure and styling\\n**Description**: Examine the React component code to understand the current structure, Bootstrap class usage, and identify areas with potential contrast issues.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**: \\n- Complete understanding of component structure and styling approach\\n- Documented list of all styled elements (cards, alerts, badges, toggles, tables, modals)\\n- Identification of Bootstrap classes being used vs custom CSS\\n- Clear mapping of problematic styling patterns\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Implementation Notes**: Focus on lines 266-267, 433-434, and 451 mentioned in requirements as potential problem areas\\n\\n### Task 2: CSS Inheritance and Override Analysis\\n**Task Name**: Audit CSS inheritance chain and custom overrides\\n**Description**: Investigate all CSS files that could affect the SelfImprovementDashboard component to identify overrides that break Bootstrap\'s text/background color relationships.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Complete audit of CSS inheritance chain for the component\\n- Documentation of all custom CSS overrides affecting text colors\\n- Identification of conflicts between Bootstrap classes and custom styles\\n- List of specific CSS rules causing contrast violations\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (Component Structure Analysis)\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Implementation Notes**: Check SelfImprovementDashboard.css, bootstrap-overrides.css, global.css, and any theme files\\n\\n### Task 3: Browser Accessibility Audit\\n**Task Name**: Perform comprehensive accessibility audit using browser dev tools\\n**Description**: Use browser developer tools accessibility features to identify all contrast violations and WCAG compliance issues.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Complete accessibility audit report from browser dev tools\\n- Documentation of all contrast ratio violations with current vs required ratios\\n- Prioritized list of violations by severity (critical/major/minor)\\n- Screenshots of problematic areas for visual reference\\n**Dependencies**: None (can run in parallel with Tasks 1-2)\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Implementation Notes**: Test in Chrome, Firefox, and Safari dev tools; focus on WCAG contrast ratio requirements (4.5:1 minimum)\\n\\n### Task 4: Element-Specific Contrast Testing\\n**Task Name**: Test contrast ratios for each UI element type\\n**Description**: Systematically test contrast ratios for all UI element categories in the component to create detailed documentation of current vs required contrast levels.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Detailed contrast testing report for each element type:\\n  - Card backgrounds (dark cards, danger cards, light cards)\\n  - Alert components (all variant types)\\n  - Badge components (all colors/variants)\\n  - Auto-apply toggle section and associated text\\n  - Table content and headers\\n  - Modal content areas\\n- Current contrast ratio measurements\\n- WCAG compliance status for each element\\n- Visual examples of readable vs unreadable combinations\\n**Dependencies**: Task 3 (Browser Accessibility Audit)\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Implementation Notes**: Use WCAG contrast checker tools for precise measurements; document both foreground and background color values\\n\\n### Task 5: Root Cause Identification\\n**Task Name**: Determine root causes of contrast violations\\n**Description**: Analyze findings from previous tasks to identify the specific reasons why text appears black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Clear identification of root causes for each type of contrast violation\\n- Documentation of whether issues stem from:\\n  - Missing Bootstrap text color classes\\n  - CSS overrides breaking Bootstrap behavior\\n  - Incorrect Bootstrap class combinations\\n  - Browser-specific rendering issues\\n  - Theme customization conflicts\\n- Prioritized list of root causes by impact and fix complexity\\n- Recommended fix strategies for each root cause type\\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 1-4 (all previous analysis tasks)\\n**Complexity**: Complex\\n**Implementation Notes**: This task synthesizes all previous analysis to create actionable insights for implementation phase\\n\\n### Task 6: Testing Strategy Definition\\n**Task Name**: Define comprehensive testing approach for readability fixes\\n**Description**: Create detailed testing strategy to ensure fixes resolve issues without introducing regressions.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Complete testing strategy document covering:\\n  - Manual visual testing checklist\\n  - Accessibility compliance verification steps\\n  - Cross-browser testing requirements\\n  - Regression testing approach\\n  - User acceptance criteria for each fix\\n- Test case specifications for each identified contrast violation\\n- Definition of success metrics and acceptance criteria\\n- Quality assurance checklist for fix validation\\n**Dependencies**: Task 5 (Root Cause Identification)\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Implementation Notes**: Focus on systematic approach to validate fixes while ensuring no functional regressions\\n\\n### Task 7: Fix Priority and Implementation Planning\\n**Task Name**: Create prioritized implementation roadmap for readability fixes\\n**Description**: Organize identified issues into a prioritized implementation plan that addresses the most critical readability problems first.\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Prioritized list of fixes organized by:\\n  - User impact (critical path elements first)\\n  - Implementation complexity (quick wins vs complex fixes)\\n  - Risk level (low-risk changes first)\\n- Detailed implementation plan for each priority level\\n- Estimated effort and timeline for each fix\\n- Dependencies between different fixes\\n- Risk assessment and mitigation strategies\\n**Dependencies**: Task 6 (Testing Strategy Definition)\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Implementation Notes**: Prepare clear handoff documentation for implementation milestone\\n\\n## Dependencies Summary\\n```\\nTask 1 (Component Analysis) \\u2192 Task 2 (CSS Override Analysis)\\nTask 3 (Accessibility Audit) \\u2192 Task 4 (Element Testing) \\nTasks 2,4 \\u2192 Task 5 (Root Cause Analysis)\\nTask 5 \\u2192 Task 6 (Testing Strategy)\\nTask 6 \\u2192 Task 7 (Implementation Planning)\\n```\\n\\n## Output Deliverables\\n1. Component structure analysis report\\n2. CSS override audit documentation\\n3. Accessibility compliance report with contrast measurements\\n4. Element-specific testing results\\n5. Root cause analysis with recommended fix strategies\\n6. Comprehensive testing strategy\\n7. Prioritized implementation roadmap\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n- Focus on Bootstrap utility classes and their proper usage\\n- Pay special attention to `text-white`, `text-dark`, `bg-dark`, `bg-light` class combinations\\n- Document specific CSS selectors and their computed styles\\n- Use browser dev tools effectively for contrast ratio testing\\n- Ensure analysis covers both component states (auto-apply enabled/disabled)\\n\\n## Success Criteria for Milestone 1\\n- Complete understanding of all readability issues in SelfImprovementDashboard\\n- Clear identification of root causes for each contrast violation\\n- Actionable implementation plan ready for development phase\\n- Comprehensive testing strategy to validate fixes\\n- No questions remaining about scope or approach for fixes"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GPjE2G2cqthnz274UgmnvK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GPjE2G2cqthnz274UgmnvK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Analysis and Architecture\\n\\n## Milestone Overview\\n**Objective**: Understand current implementation and identify specific CSS/styling issues causing readability problems on the Improve page (SelfImprovementDashboard component).\\n\\n**Note**: This milestone is primarily frontend-focused as it deals with UI readability issues. However, there are backend considerations for data structure analysis and potential API adjustments.\\n\\n## Backend Analysis Tasks\\n\\n### Task 1: Data Model Analysis\\n**Description**: Analyze the data structures and API responses that feed the SelfImprovementDashboard to understand how data attributes affect styling decisions.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Document all data models used by SelfImprovementDashboard\\n- Identify conditional styling logic based on data values\\n- Map data fields to UI styling decisions\\n- Document API endpoints serving the dashboard\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Estimated Time**: 1-2 hours\\n\\n### Task 2: API Response Structure Review\\n**Description**: Review existing API responses for improvement suggestions, auto-apply settings, and any data that determines UI states affecting readability.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Document current API endpoints used by SelfImprovementDashboard\\n- Analyze response structures for styling-related fields\\n- Identify any backend logic that affects UI state\\n- Document data flow from backend to frontend styling\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Estimated Time**: 1-2 hours\\n\\n### Task 3: Backend Configuration Analysis\\n**Description**: Examine backend configuration or settings that might affect frontend themes, dark mode settings, or styling preferences.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Check for any backend-stored user preferences affecting UI themes\\n- Document configuration options that impact frontend styling\\n- Identify any backend logic for theme/styling management\\n- Review environment variables or config files affecting UI\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Estimated Time**: 1 hour\\n\\n## Frontend Analysis Tasks (For Reference - Not Backend)\\n\\n### Task 4: Component Code Review\\n**Description**: Analyze SelfImprovementDashboard component code to identify readability issues.\\n**Note**: This would be handled by Frontend Coordinator, not backend.\\n\\n### Task 5: CSS/Styling Investigation\\n**Description**: Investigate Bootstrap theme overrides and custom CSS causing contrast issues.\\n**Note**: This would be handled by Frontend Coordinator, not backend.\\n\\n### Task 6: Accessibility Audit\\n**Description**: Perform WCAG contrast ratio testing on problematic UI elements.\\n**Note**: This would be handled by Frontend Coordinator, not backend.\\n\\n## Backend Support Tasks\\n\\n### Task 7: Theme Data Structure Design\\n**Description**: If user theme preferences need to be stored backend, design data structure for theme/styling preferences.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Design user preference schema for UI themes\\n- Plan API endpoints for theme preference management\\n- Consider dark mode, contrast settings, accessibility preferences\\n- Design backward compatibility approach\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 1-3\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Estimated Time**: 2-3 hours\\n**Status**: Optional (only if backend theme storage needed)\\n\\n### Task 8: API Enhancement Planning\\n**Description**: Plan any backend API enhancements needed to support improved frontend styling logic.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Identify API additions needed for theme support\\n- Plan data structure modifications for better styling support\\n- Design API versioning strategy if changes needed\\n- Document migration path for existing data\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 7\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Estimated Time**: 2-3 hours\\n**Status**: Optional (only if API changes needed)\\n\\n## Task Dependencies\\n\\n```\\nTask 1 (Data Model Analysis)\\n    \\u2193\\nTask 2 (API Response Review)\\n    \\u2193\\nTask 3 (Backend Config Analysis)\\n    \\u2193\\n[Optional] Task 7 (Theme Data Structure)\\n    \\u2193\\n[Optional] Task 8 (API Enhancement Planning)\\n```\\n\\n## Priority Order\\n\\n1. **High Priority**: Tasks 1-3 (Analysis and documentation)\\n2. **Medium Priority**: Tasks 7-8 (Only if backend changes needed)\\n\\n## Expected Outcomes\\n\\nFrom the backend perspective, this milestone should produce:\\n\\n1. **Documentation** of current data flow affecting UI styling\\n2. **Analysis** of any backend configuration impacting frontend themes\\n3. **Recommendations** for backend changes (if any) to support improved UI\\n4. **Data structure designs** (if theme preferences need backend storage)\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n\\n- **Primary Issue**: Frontend CSS/styling problem, minimal backend involvement expected\\n- **Backend Role**: Support analysis and provide foundation for any theme management features\\n- **API Stability**: Existing APIs should remain functional during UI fixes\\n- **Data Integrity**: No data migrations expected for pure styling fixes\\n\\n## Ready for Implementation\\n\\nThese tasks are ready to be implemented by the TDD Coordinator using test-driven development approach. Each task has clear acceptance criteria and can be validated through automated tests."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TAVHgRFiUnK2JFR1jfkst1', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TAVHgRFiUnK2JFR1jfkst1', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy - Milestone 1: Analysis and Investigation\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis milestone focuses on identifying all readability issues and their root causes in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The goal is thorough analysis and documentation of contrast violations before implementing fixes.\\n\\n## Test Categories\\n\\n### 1. Visual Regression Tests\\n**Purpose**: Detect current readability issues and establish baseline\\n**Tools**: Playwright for visual testing, axe-core for accessibility\\n\\n#### Test Tasks:\\n\\n**Task 1.1: Screenshot Baseline Tests**\\n- Create screenshots of SelfImprovementDashboard in all states:\\n  - Auto-apply disabled (light mode)\\n  - Auto-apply enabled (danger mode) \\n  - Modal dialogs open\\n  - Different card states\\n  - Loading states\\n- Store as baseline for regression detection\\n- Coverage: Visual state coverage\\n\\n**Task 1.2: Contrast Ratio Analysis**\\n- Programmatically test all text elements for WCAG AA compliance (4.5:1 ratio)\\n- Test color combinations:\\n  - bg-dark with default text\\n  - bg-danger with white text\\n  - bg-light with dark text\\n  - Card headers and bodies\\n  - Table content\\n  - Modal content\\n- Identify specific failing elements\\n- Coverage: Accessibility compliance\\n\\n### 2. Component Integration Tests\\n**Purpose**: Verify component rendering and state management\\n**Tools**: React Testing Library, Jest\\n\\n#### Test Tasks:\\n\\n**Task 2.1: Bootstrap Class Application Tests**\\n- Test that correct Bootstrap classes are applied:\\n  - `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` combinations\\n  - `bg=\\"danger\\" text=\\"white\\"` combinations\\n  - `bg=\\"light\\" text=\\"dark\\"` combinations\\n- Verify conditional styling logic works correctly\\n- Test auto-apply toggle state changes\\n- Coverage: Component state and styling logic\\n\\n**Task 2.2: CSS Override Detection Tests**\\n- Test for conflicting CSS rules that override Bootstrap classes\\n- Check computed styles match expected Bootstrap values\\n- Identify custom CSS that may cause contrast issues\\n- Test CSS cascade and specificity problems\\n- Coverage: Style inheritance and overrides\\n\\n### 3. User Experience Tests\\n**Purpose**: Simulate real user interactions with readability issues\\n**Tools**: Playwright E2E tests\\n\\n#### Test Tasks:\\n\\n**Task 3.1: User Journey Readability Tests**\\n- Navigate through all sections of SelfImprovementDashboard\\n- Attempt to read all text elements\\n- Test in different browser environments\\n- Simulate different display settings (zoom, font size)\\n- Coverage: End-to-end user experience\\n\\n**Task 3.2: Cross-Browser Contrast Tests**\\n- Test rendering in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n- Test on different operating systems\\n- Check for browser-specific rendering issues\\n- Verify font rendering consistency\\n- Coverage: Browser compatibility\\n\\n### 4. Accessibility Audit Tests\\n**Purpose**: Comprehensive accessibility evaluation\\n**Tools**: axe-core, manual testing\\n\\n#### Test Tasks:\\n\\n**Task 4.1: Automated Accessibility Testing**\\n- Run axe-core accessibility tests\\n- Check for WCAG violations beyond contrast\\n- Test keyboard navigation\\n- Verify screen reader compatibility\\n- Coverage: Full accessibility compliance\\n\\n**Task 4.2: Manual Accessibility Testing**\\n- Manual review with screen reader software\\n- Test with high contrast mode enabled\\n- Verify color-blind accessibility\\n- Test with system dark mode\\n- Coverage: Real-world accessibility scenarios\\n\\n## Test Infrastructure\\n\\n### Setup Requirements\\n- Playwright for browser automation\\n- Jest + React Testing Library for component tests\\n- axe-core for accessibility testing\\n- Color contrast analyzer tools\\n- Multiple browsers for cross-platform testing\\n\\n### Test Data\\n- Component props for different states\\n- Mock data for dashboard content\\n- Various viewport sizes\\n- Different theme configurations\\n\\n### Coverage Goals\\n- **Visual Coverage**: 100% of UI states captured\\n- **Contrast Testing**: All text/background combinations analyzed\\n- **Component Coverage**: All rendering paths tested\\n- **Accessibility Coverage**: WCAG AA compliance verified\\n- **Browser Coverage**: Chrome, Firefox, Safari tested\\n\\n## Expected Deliverables\\n\\n### 1. Readability Issues Report\\n- Comprehensive list of all contrast violations\\n- Screenshots showing problematic areas\\n- Specific CSS classes/elements affected\\n- WCAG compliance analysis\\n\\n### 2. Root Cause Analysis\\n- Identification of CSS overrides causing issues\\n- Bootstrap class conflicts\\n- Theme customization problems\\n- Browser-specific rendering issues\\n\\n### 3. Test Suite Implementation\\n- Automated contrast testing\\n- Visual regression tests\\n- Component integration tests\\n- Accessibility audit tests\\n\\n### 4. Baseline Documentation\\n- Current state screenshots\\n- Contrast ratio measurements\\n- Accessibility audit results\\n- Browser compatibility matrix\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- \\u2705 All readability issues identified and documented\\n- \\u2705 Root causes clearly understood\\n- \\u2705 Comprehensive test suite implemented\\n- \\u2705 Baseline established for future regression testing\\n- \\u2705 Ready to proceed to fix implementation phase\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **False Positives**: Manual review of automated contrast findings\\n- **Browser Differences**: Test on multiple browsers/OS combinations\\n- **Dynamic Content**: Test all possible component states\\n- **Theme Dependencies**: Test with different Bootstrap theme configurations\\n\\nThis analysis phase ensures we thoroughly understand the problem scope before implementing fixes, preventing incomplete solutions and regression issues."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011wTwNcBzSHjjd4idrCTeap', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui -name "*SelfImprovementDashboard*" -o -name "*RecoveryDashboard*" -o -name "*Improve*" -type f'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011wTwNcBzSHjjd4idrCTeap', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx\\n/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.jsx\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011eUMkxtZttDjeR2FM32zTp', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011eUMkxtZttDjeR2FM32zTp', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\nimport { Container, Row, Col, Card, Table, Spinner, Button, Badge, Alert, Form, Modal } from \'react-bootstrap\';\\n\\nconst API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || \'http://localhost:8001\';\\n\\nfunction RecoveryDashboard() {\\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\\n  const [stalledAgents, setStalledAgents] = useState([]);\\n  const [recoveryQueue, setRecoveryQueue] = useState(null);\\n  const [recoveryHistory, setRecoveryHistory] = useState([]);\\n  const [scanResult, setScanResult] = useState(null);\\n  const [scanning, setScanning] = useState(false);\\n  const [showRecoveryModal, setShowRecoveryModal] = useState(false);\\n  const [selectedAgent, setSelectedAgent] = useState(null);\\n  const [selectedStrategy, setSelectedStrategy] = useState(\'retry\');\\n  const [actionInProgress, setActionInProgress] = useState(null);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    fetchRecoveryData();\\n    const interval = setInterval(fetchRecoveryData, 5000); // Poll every 5 seconds\\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const fetchRecoveryData = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      const [stalledRes, queueRes, historyRes] = await Promise.all([\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/recovery/stalled`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/recovery/queue`),\\n        fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/recovery/history?limit=50`)\\n      ]);\\n\\n      // Check all responses\\n      if (!stalledRes.ok || !queueRes.ok || !historyRes.ok) {\\n        throw new Error(\'One or more API calls failed\');\\n      }\\n\\n      const stalledData = await stalledRes.json();\\n      const queueData = await queueRes.json();\\n      const historyData = await historyRes.json();\\n\\n      setStalledAgents(stalledData.stalled_agents || []);\\n      setRecoveryQueue(queueData);\\n      setRecoveryHistory(historyData.history || []);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to fetch recovery data:\', error);\\n      // Set safe defaults on error\\n      setStalledAgents([]);\\n      setRecoveryQueue({ pending_tasks: [] });\\n      setRecoveryHistory([]);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleScan = async () => {\\n    setScanning(true);\\n    setScanResult(null);\\n    try {\\n      const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/recovery/scan`, { method: \'POST\' });\\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\\n      const result = await response.json();\\n      setScanResult(result);\\n      await fetchRecoveryData(); // Refresh data\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      console.error(\'Scan failed:\', error);\\n      setScanResult({ error: \'Scan failed\' });\\n    } finally {\\n      setScanning(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleTriggerRecovery = async () => {\\n    if (!selectedAgent) return;\\n\\n    setActionInProgress(selectedAgent);\\n    try {\\n      const response = await fetch(\\n        `${API_BASE}/api/recovery/trigger/${selectedAgent}?strategy=${selectedStrategy}`,\\n        { method: \'POST\' }\\n      );\\n      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\\n      const result = await response.json();\\n      if (result.success) {\\n        await fetchRecoveryData();\\n      }\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      console.error(\'Recovery trigger failed:\', error);\\n    } finally {\\n      setActionInProgress(null);\\n      setShowRecoveryModal(false);\\n      setSelectedAgent(null);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const openRecoveryModal = (agentId) => {\\n    setSelectedAgent(agentId);\\n    setSelectedStrategy(\'retry\');\\n    setShowRecoveryModal(true);\\n  };\\n\\n  const getStrategyBadge = (strategy) => {\\n    const colors = {\\n      \'retry\': \'primary\',\\n      \'retry_backoff\': \'info\',\\n      \'enhance_prompt\': \'warning\',\\n      \'refactor_agent\': \'secondary\',\\n      \'escalate_model\': \'danger\',\\n      \'manual\': \'dark\'\\n    };\\n    return <Badge bg={colors[strategy] || \'secondary\'}>{strategy}</Badge>;\\n  };\\n\\n  const getStatusBadge = (status) => {\\n    const colors = {\\n      \'pending\': \'warning\',\\n      \'in_progress\': \'primary\',\\n      \'completed\': \'success\',\\n      \'failed\': \'danger\',\\n      \'needs_review\': \'info\',\\n      \'aborted\': \'dark\'\\n    };\\n    return <Badge bg={colors[status] || \'secondary\'}>{status}</Badge>;\\n  };\\n\\n  const formatTimestamp = (timestamp) => {\\n    if (!timestamp) return \'N/A\';\\n    return new Date(timestamp).toLocaleString();\\n  };\\n\\n  const formatDuration = (ms) => {\\n    if (!ms) return \'N/A\';\\n    if (ms < 1000) return `${ms}ms`;\\n    if (ms < 60000) return `${(ms/1000).toFixed(1)}s`;\\n    return `${(ms/60000).toFixed(1)}m`;\\n  };\\n\\n  if (loading) {\\n    return (\\n      <Container className=\\"mt-5 text-center\\">\\n        <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" variant=\\"warning\\" />\\n        <p className=\\"mt-3\\" style={{ color: \'#e4e6eb\' }}>Loading recovery data...</p>\\n      </Container>\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  const activeRecoveries = recoveryQueue?.active_recoveries || [];\\n  const pendingTasks = recoveryQueue?.pending_tasks || [];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <Container fluid className=\\"mt-4\\" style={{ color: \'#e4e6eb\' }}>\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <h2>Recovery Dashboard</h2>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col xs=\\"auto\\">\\n          <Button\\n            variant=\\"warning\\"\\n            onClick={handleScan}\\n            disabled={scanning}\\n          >\\n            {scanning ? (\\n              <>\\n                <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"me-2\\" />\\n                Scanning...\\n              </>\\n            ) : (\\n              \'Scan for Stalled Agents\'\\n            )}\\n          </Button>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {scanResult && (\\n        <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n          <Col>\\n            <Alert variant={scanResult.error ? \'danger\' : \'info\'} dismissible onClose={() => setScanResult(null)}>\\n              {scanResult.error ? (\\n                scanResult.error\\n              ) : (\\n                <>\\n                  <strong>Scan Complete:</strong> Found {scanResult.stalled_count} stalled agent(s),\\n                  queued {scanResult.queued_for_recovery} for recovery.\\n                </>\\n              )}\\n            </Alert>\\n          </Col>\\n        </Row>\\n      )}\\n\\n      {/* Status Cards */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card style={{ background: \'linear-gradient(135deg, #ef4444 0%, #dc2626 100%)\', color: \'white\' }}>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Stalled Agents\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{stalledAgents.length}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card style={{ background: \'linear-gradient(135deg, #f59e0b 0%, #d97706 100%)\', color: \'white\' }}>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                In Recovery Queue\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{pendingTasks.length}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card style={{ background: \'linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6 0%, #1d4ed8 100%)\', color: \'white\' }}>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Active Recoveries\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{activeRecoveries.length}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={3}>\\n          <Card style={{ background: recoveryQueue?.is_running ? \'linear-gradient(135deg, #10b981 0%, #059669 100%)\' : \'linear-gradient(135deg, #6b7280 0%, #4b5563 100%)\', color: \'white\' }}>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.75rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                System Status\\n              </h6>\\n              <h3 className=\\"mb-0\\">{recoveryQueue?.is_running ? \'Active\' : \'Stopped\'}</h3>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Active Recoveries */}\\n      {activeRecoveries.length > 0 && (\\n        <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n          <Col>\\n            <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n              <Card.Header>\\n                <strong>Active Recoveries</strong>\\n                <Badge bg=\\"primary\\" className=\\"ms-2\\">{activeRecoveries.length}</Badge>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              <Card.Body>\\n                <div style={{ display: \'flex\', gap: \'12px\', flexWrap: \'wrap\' }}>\\n                  {activeRecoveries.map((agentId, idx) => (\\n                    <div\\n                      key={idx}\\n                      style={{\\n                        padding: \'8px 16px\',\\n                        backgroundColor: \'#2563eb\',\\n                        borderRadius: \'6px\',\\n                        display: \'flex\',\\n                        alignItems: \'center\',\\n                        gap: \'8px\'\\n                      }}\\n                    >\\n                      <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" />\\n                      <code>{agentId}</code>\\n                    </div>\\n                  ))}\\n                </div>\\n              </Card.Body>\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n        </Row>\\n      )}\\n\\n      {/* Stalled Agents */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>Stalled Agents</strong>\\n              <Badge bg=\\"danger\\" className=\\"ms-2\\">{stalledAgents.length}</Badge>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              {stalledAgents.length === 0 ? (\\n                <div className=\\"text-center py-4\\" style={{ color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n                  No stalled agents detected\\n                </div>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Table hover size=\\"sm\\" variant=\\"dark\\">\\n                  <thead>\\n                    <tr>\\n                      <th>Agent</th>\\n                      <th>Reason</th>\\n                      <th>Duration</th>\\n                      <th>Action</th>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  </thead>\\n                  <tbody>\\n                    {stalledAgents.map((agent, idx) => (\\n                      <tr key={idx}>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{agent.agent_name || agent.agent_id}</code>\\n                          <br />\\n                          <small style={{ color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>{agent.agent_type}</small>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\">{agent.stall_reason || \'unknown\'}</Badge>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          {agent.stall_duration_ms ? formatDuration(agent.stall_duration_ms) : \'N/A\'}\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Button\\n                            size=\\"sm\\"\\n                            variant=\\"outline-warning\\"\\n                            onClick={() => openRecoveryModal(agent.agent_id)}\\n                            disabled={actionInProgress === agent.agent_id}\\n                          >\\n                            {actionInProgress === agent.agent_id ? (\\n                              <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" />\\n                            ) : (\\n                              \'Recover\'\\n                            )}\\n                          </Button>\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </tbody>\\n                </Table>\\n              )}\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n\\n        {/* Recovery Queue */}\\n        <Col md={6}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>Recovery Queue</strong>\\n              <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" className=\\"ms-2\\">{pendingTasks.length}</Badge>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'400px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              {pendingTasks.length === 0 ? (\\n                <div className=\\"text-center py-4\\" style={{ color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n                  Recovery queue is empty\\n                </div>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Table hover size=\\"sm\\" variant=\\"dark\\">\\n                  <thead>\\n                    <tr>\\n                      <th>Agent</th>\\n                      <th>Strategy</th>\\n                      <th>Reason</th>\\n                      <th>Attempts</th>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  </thead>\\n                  <tbody>\\n                    {pendingTasks.map((task, idx) => (\\n                      <tr key={idx}>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{task.agent_name || task.agent_id}</code>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>{getStrategyBadge(task.strategy)}</td>\\n                        <td style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{task.reason}</td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Badge bg=\\"secondary\\">{task.attempts || 0}</Badge>\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </tbody>\\n                </Table>\\n              )}\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Recovery History */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>Recovery History</strong>\\n              <Badge bg=\\"info\\" className=\\"ms-2\\">{recoveryHistory.length}</Badge>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'500px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              {recoveryHistory.length === 0 ? (\\n                <div className=\\"text-center py-4\\" style={{ color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n                  No recovery history available\\n                </div>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Table hover size=\\"sm\\" variant=\\"dark\\">\\n                  <thead>\\n                    <tr>\\n                      <th>Agent</th>\\n                      <th>Type</th>\\n                      <th>Strategy</th>\\n                      <th>Status</th>\\n                      <th>Reason</th>\\n                      <th>Attempts</th>\\n                      <th>Time</th>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  </thead>\\n                  <tbody>\\n                    {recoveryHistory.map((record, idx) => (\\n                      <tr key={idx}>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <code style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{record.agent_name || record.agent_id}</code>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\' }}>{record.agent_type}</td>\\n                        <td>{getStrategyBadge(record.recovery_strategy)}</td>\\n                        <td>{getStatusBadge(record.status)}</td>\\n                        <td style={{ fontSize: \'0.85rem\', maxWidth: \'200px\', overflow: \'hidden\', textOverflow: \'ellipsis\' }}>\\n                          {record.recovery_reason}\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Badge bg=\\"secondary\\">{record.attempts || 0}/{record.max_attempts || 5}</Badge>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td style={{ fontSize: \'0.8rem\' }}>\\n                          {formatTimestamp(record.created_at)}\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </tbody>\\n                </Table>\\n              )}\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Recovery Strategies Reference */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"light\\">\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>Recovery Strategies Reference</strong>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <Row>\\n                <Col md={6}>\\n                  <ul className=\\"mb-0\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.9rem\' }}>\\n                    <li><strong>retry:</strong> Simple retry with same parameters</li>\\n                    <li><strong>retry_backoff:</strong> Retry with exponential backoff delay</li>\\n                    <li><strong>enhance_prompt:</strong> Improve prompt clarity before retrying</li>\\n                  </ul>\\n                </Col>\\n                <Col md={6}>\\n                  <ul className=\\"mb-0\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.9rem\' }}>\\n                    <li><strong>refactor_agent:</strong> Update agent definition with guardrails</li>\\n                    <li><strong>escalate_model:</strong> Retry with more powerful model (Haiku-&gt;Sonnet-&gt;Opus)</li>\\n                    <li><strong>manual:</strong> Flag for human review and intervention</li>\\n                  </ul>\\n                </Col>\\n              </Row>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Recovery Modal */}\\n      <Modal show={showRecoveryModal} onHide={() => setShowRecoveryModal(false)} centered>\\n        <Modal.Header closeButton style={{ backgroundColor: \'#242836\', color: \'#e4e6eb\', borderColor: \'#3a3f52\' }}>\\n          <Modal.Title>Trigger Recovery</Modal.Title>\\n        </Modal.Header>\\n        <Modal.Body style={{ backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\', color: \'#e4e6eb\' }}>\\n          <p>Agent: <code>{selectedAgent}</code></p>\\n          <Form.Group>\\n            <Form.Label>Recovery Strategy</Form.Label>\\n            <Form.Select\\n              value={selectedStrategy}\\n              onChange={(e) => setSelectedStrategy(e.target.value)}\\n              style={{\\n                backgroundColor: \'#242836\',\\n                color: \'#e4e6eb\',\\n                borderColor: \'#3a3f52\'\\n              }}\\n            >\\n              <option value=\\"retry\\">Retry (simple retry)</option>\\n              <option value=\\"retry_backoff\\">Retry with Backoff</option>\\n              <option value=\\"enhance_prompt\\">Enhance Prompt</option>\\n              <option value=\\"refactor_agent\\">Refactor Agent</option>\\n              <option value=\\"escalate_model\\">Escalate Model</option>\\n              <option value=\\"manual\\">Manual Intervention</option>\\n            </Form.Select>\\n          </Form.Group>\\n        </Modal.Body>\\n        <Modal.Footer style={{ backgroundColor: \'#242836\', borderColor: \'#3a3f52\' }}>\\n          <Button variant=\\"secondary\\" onClick={() => setShowRecoveryModal(false)}>\\n            Cancel\\n          </Button>\\n          <Button variant=\\"warning\\" onClick={handleTriggerRecovery}>\\n            Start Recovery\\n          </Button>\\n        </Modal.Footer>\\n      </Modal>\\n    </Container>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default RecoveryDashboard;\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DRJT4RwKXuYcJHRehqntCA', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'testers/unit_test_lead', 'input_data': {'task': 'Write comprehensive unit tests to analyze and identify all readability issues in the RecoveryDashboard component. Tests should verify contrast ratios, identify dark background/dark text combinations, and document all styling-related issues that make text unreadable.', 'test_file': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.test.jsx', 'code_file': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.jsx', 'requirements': 'Create tests that identify readability issues where text appears black on dark backgrounds. Focus on Bootstrap class combinations, inline styles, and computed CSS that causes poor contrast. Tests should fail initially to document current readability problems, establishing a baseline for fixes.'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DRJT4RwKXuYcJHRehqntCA', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01StyZMt68A2muw6wD2grcwc', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.test.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01StyZMt68A2muw6wD2grcwc', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/RecoveryDashboard.test.jsx"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
