{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:57:21", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6e579436-bd2e-4427-9b1f-46f4968e8dca', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Analysis and investigation of readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component where black text appears on dark backgrounds. Need to systematically identify all contrast violations, audit CSS inheritance, analyze component structure, test accessibility compliance, and determine root causes before implementing fixes.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GXPYqnBH5iASYnevA4bv8Z', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'SelfImprovementDashboard Readability Analysis', 'description': 'Analysis and investigation of readability issues where black text appears on dark backgrounds'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GXPYqnBH5iASYnevA4bv8Z', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "60f45a3a", "message": "Created project: SelfImprovementDashboard Readability Analysis", "summary": {"project_id": "60f45a3a", "project_name": "SelfImprovementDashboard Readability Analysis", "description": "Analysis and investigation of readability issues where black text appears on dark backgrounds", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-14T21:53:45.423403", "updated_at": "2026-01-14T21:53:45.423403", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-14T21:53:45.423403", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'SelfImprovementDashboard Readability Analysis\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NvAhzEnW4CeGNS7JfZwEiA', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NvAhzEnW4CeGNS7JfZwEiA', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Fix the unreadable text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) where black text appears on dark backgrounds, making it nearly impossible to read.\\n\\n**Problem**: Users report that the Improve page has severe readability issues with black text on dark backgrounds, creating a poor user experience and making the interface unusable in some areas.\\n\\n**Solution**: Identify and fix all instances of poor contrast between text and background colors to ensure proper readability across all UI elements.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Core Requirements\\n1. **Readability Fix**: Ensure all text on the Improve page is readable with proper contrast\\n2. **Bootstrap Consistency**: Maintain Bootstrap theme consistency while fixing contrast issues\\n3. **Dark Mode Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work properly in both light and dark mode contexts\\n4. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG guidelines for text contrast (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text)\\n\\n### Specific Issues to Address\\n1. **Card Backgrounds**: Review all Card components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` and ensure text is white/light\\n2. **Alert Styling**: Ensure Alert components have proper text contrast\\n3. **Badge Colors**: Verify Badge components maintain readability\\n4. **Auto-Apply Toggle**: Check styling of the toggle switch and associated text\\n5. **Table Content**: Ensure table text is readable against backgrounds\\n6. **Modal Content**: Verify modal text readability\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Cannot break existing functionality\\n- Must preserve current color scheme intent (danger/warning/success indicators)\\n- Should use Bootstrap\'s built-in text color classes where possible\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page is readable with adequate contrast\\n2. No functionality is broken by the styling changes\\n3. Design maintains visual hierarchy and color-coded meanings\\n4. Changes are minimal and focused on contrast fixes only\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to other pages\\n- Functionality modifications\\n- Theme system overhaul\\n\\n## Analysis of Current Issues\\nBased on the SelfImprovementDashboard code review, potential problem areas:\\n\\n1. **Lines 266-267**: `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` - This should be correct\\n2. **Lines 433-434**: Card with conditional background (`bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}`) - Light background with dark text should be readable\\n3. **Lines 451**: `bg-dark` class usage in auto-apply warning section\\n\\nThe issue might be in CSS overrides or Bootstrap theme customization that\'s causing text to appear black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes being used.\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- User is referring to the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page)\\n- Issue is with CSS/styling, not functional behavior\\n- Bootstrap framework is being used correctly in most places\\n- Problem may be in CSS overrides or theme customization\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n1. Analyze current styling and identify specific contrast violations\\n2. Fix styling issues using appropriate Bootstrap classes or custom CSS\\n3. Test readability across different states (auto-apply on/off, different card states)\\n4. Ensure accessibility compliance\\n5. Verify no regressions in functionality or other visual elements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017DKstBnMDNPguCfyjNqL71', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '60f45a3a', 'description': 'Identify and audit all contrast violations in SelfImprovementDashboard component', 'assigned_to': 'testers/unit_test_lead'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017DKstBnMDNPguCfyjNqL71', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "7d104422", "message": "Added task: Identify and audit all contrast violations in SelfImprovementDashboard component"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018A6nAP59bkFETK8aWZ8M5z', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '60f45a3a', 'description': 'Analyze CSS inheritance and Bootstrap theme overrides affecting text visibility', 'assigned_to': 'developers/frontend_lead'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018A6nAP59bkFETK8aWZ8M5z', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "97c270ee", "message": "Added task: Analyze CSS inheritance and Bootstrap theme overrides affecting text visibility"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CR4Evrv1Sc9TT4aHQqEfCd', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '60f45a3a', 'description': 'Test accessibility compliance and contrast ratios for WCAG guidelines', 'assigned_to': 'testers/integration_test_lead'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CR4Evrv1Sc9TT4aHQqEfCd', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "2723deb9", "message": "Added task: Test accessibility compliance and contrast ratios for WCAG guidelines"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RGaGSTQacFyY9Bj54KLqRb', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '60f45a3a', 'description': 'Create comprehensive test plan for validating readability fixes', 'assigned_to': 'testers/unit_test_lead'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RGaGSTQacFyY9Bj54KLqRb', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "82bc6ce1", "message": "Added task: Create comprehensive test plan for validating readability fixes"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AUkNLj2weFsbSA4M2xasFv', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'testers/unit_test_lead', 'input_data': {'task': 'Create comprehensive test suite to identify contrast violations in SelfImprovementDashboard component', 'test_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx', 'code_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx', 'requirements': 'Test should validate proper contrast ratios (4.5:1 minimum), check for dark text on dark backgrounds, verify Bootstrap class usage, and audit all card backgrounds, alerts, badges, and table elements for readability issues', 'test_type': 'accessibility_contrast'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AUkNLj2weFsbSA4M2xasFv', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014Zz92mPaVji6nqMPMDL4R8', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014Zz92mPaVji6nqMPMDL4R8', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AV26RsNw7X1kNep1M2xmnQ', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble -name "*SelfImprovement*" -type f'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AV26RsNw7X1kNep1M2xmnQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PJismkpHb15TZAeTavwuXV', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PJismkpHb15TZAeTavwuXV', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\nimport { Container, Row, Col, Card, Table, Spinner, Button, Badge, Alert, Modal, Form } from \'react-bootstrap\';\\nimport {\\n  getSelfImprovementStatus,\\n  runSelfImprovementAnalysis,\\n  getRecommendations,\\n  approveRecommendation,\\n  rejectRecommendation,\\n  getAutoApplyConfig,\\n  setAutoApplyConfig,\\n  applyAllRecommendations,\\n  applySingleRecommendation\\n} from \'../services/api\';\\n\\nconst API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || \'http://localhost:8001\';\\n\\nfunction SelfImprovementDashboard() {\\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\\n  const [analyzing, setAnalyzing] = useState(false);\\n  const [applying, setApplying] = useState(false);\\n  const [status, setStatus] = useState(null);\\n  const [recommendations, setRecommendations] = useState([]);\\n  const [analysis, setAnalysis] = useState(null);\\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\\n  const [showRejectModal, setShowRejectModal] = useState(false);\\n  const [selectedRec, setSelectedRec] = useState(null);\\n  const [rejectReason, setRejectReason] = useState(\'\');\\n  const [autoApplyEnabled, setAutoApplyEnabled] = useState(false);\\n  const [autoApplyConfig, setAutoApplyConfigState] = useState(null);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    fetchData();\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const fetchData = async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const [statusRes, recsRes, autoApplyRes] = await Promise.all([\\n        getSelfImprovementStatus(),\\n        getRecommendations(),\\n        getAutoApplyConfig()\\n      ]);\\n      setStatus(statusRes);\\n      setRecommendations(recsRes.recommendations || []);\\n      setAutoApplyConfigState(autoApplyRes);\\n      setAutoApplyEnabled(autoApplyRes?.enabled || false);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to fetch self-improvement data:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to load self-improvement data. Is the backend running?\');\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleRunAnalysis = async () => {\\n    setAnalyzing(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const result = await runSelfImprovementAnalysis(30);\\n      setAnalysis(result);\\n      // Refresh recommendations after analysis\\n      const recsRes = await getRecommendations();\\n      setRecommendations(recsRes.recommendations || []);\\n      // Refresh status\\n      const statusRes = await getSelfImprovementStatus();\\n      setStatus(statusRes);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to run analysis:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to run analysis. Check console for details.\');\\n    } finally {\\n      setAnalyzing(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleApprove = async (recId) => {\\n    try {\\n      await approveRecommendation(recId);\\n      // Refresh data\\n      await fetchData();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to approve recommendation:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to approve recommendation\');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleReject = async () => {\\n    if (!selectedRec) return;\\n    try {\\n      await rejectRecommendation(selectedRec.id, rejectReason);\\n      setShowRejectModal(false);\\n      setSelectedRec(null);\\n      setRejectReason(\'\');\\n      // Refresh data\\n      await fetchData();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to reject recommendation:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to reject recommendation\');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const openRejectModal = (rec) => {\\n    setSelectedRec(rec);\\n    setShowRejectModal(true);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleToggleAutoApply = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      const newEnabled = !autoApplyEnabled;\\n      await setAutoApplyConfig(newEnabled, true, \'medium\');\\n      setAutoApplyEnabled(newEnabled);\\n      // Refresh config\\n      const configRes = await getAutoApplyConfig();\\n      setAutoApplyConfigState(configRes);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to toggle auto-apply:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to toggle auto-apply mode\');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleApplyAll = async () => {\\n    setApplying(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const result = await applyAllRecommendations();\\n      setAnalysis(prev => ({\\n        ...prev,\\n        auto_apply_results: result.results\\n      }));\\n      // Refresh data\\n      await fetchData();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to apply all recommendations:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to apply recommendations\');\\n    } finally {\\n      setApplying(false);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleApplySingle = async (recId) => {\\n    try {\\n      await applySingleRecommendation(recId);\\n      await fetchData();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to apply recommendation:\', err);\\n      setError(\'Failed to apply recommendation\');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const getPriorityBadge = (priority) => {\\n    const colors = {\\n      critical: \'danger\',\\n      high: \'warning\',\\n      medium: \'info\',\\n      low: \'secondary\'\\n    };\\n    return <Badge bg={colors[priority] || \'secondary\'}>{priority}</Badge>;\\n  };\\n\\n  const getTypeBadge = (type) => {\\n    const labels = {\\n      model_upgrade: \'Model Upgrade\',\\n      model_downgrade: \'Cost Optimization\',\\n      definition_tweak: \'Definition Tweak\',\\n      definition_major: \'Major Rewrite\',\\n      iteration_increase: \'More Iterations\',\\n      iteration_decrease: \'Fewer Iterations\',\\n      complexity_change: \'Complexity Change\',\\n      alert: \'Alert\'\\n    };\\n    return <Badge bg=\\"dark\\">{labels[type] || type}</Badge>;\\n  };\\n\\n  if (loading) {\\n    return (\\n      <Container className=\\"mt-5 text-center\\">\\n        <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" variant=\\"primary\\" />\\n        <p className=\\"mt-3\\">Loading self-improvement data...</p>\\n      </Container>\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <Container fluid className=\\"mt-4\\">\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <h2>Self-Improvement Loop</h2>\\n          <p className=\\"text-muted\\">\\n            The self-improvement loop analyzes agent performance and generates recommendations for improvement.\\n            Feedback is automatically injected into agent prompts to help them learn from past performance.\\n          </p>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col xs=\\"auto\\" className=\\"d-flex align-items-center gap-3\\">\\n          {/* Auto-Apply Toggle */}\\n          <div className=\\"d-flex align-items-center\\">\\n            <Form.Check\\n              type=\\"switch\\"\\n              id=\\"auto-apply-switch\\"\\n              label=\\"\\"\\n              checked={autoApplyEnabled}\\n              onChange={handleToggleAutoApply}\\n              className=\\"me-2\\"\\n              style={{ transform: \'scale(1.3)\' }}\\n            />\\n            <span\\n              className={`fw-bold ${autoApplyEnabled ? \'text-danger\' : \'text-muted\'}`}\\n              style={{ cursor: \'pointer\' }}\\n              onClick={handleToggleAutoApply}\\n            >\\n              {autoApplyEnabled ? \'BUMPERS OFF\' : \'Bumpers On\'}\\n            </span>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Apply All Button */}\\n          {recommendations.length > 0 && (\\n            <Button\\n              variant={autoApplyEnabled ? \\"danger\\" : \\"warning\\"}\\n              onClick={handleApplyAll}\\n              disabled={applying}\\n            >\\n              {applying ? (\\n                <>\\n                  <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"me-2\\" />\\n                  Applying...\\n                </>\\n              ) : (\\n                `Apply All (${recommendations.length})`\\n              )}\\n            </Button>\\n          )}\\n\\n          <Button\\n            variant=\\"primary\\"\\n            onClick={handleRunAnalysis}\\n            disabled={analyzing}\\n          >\\n            {analyzing ? (\\n              <>\\n                <Spinner animation=\\"border\\" size=\\"sm\\" className=\\"me-2\\" />\\n                Analyzing...\\n              </>\\n            ) : (\\n              \'Run Analysis\'\\n            )}\\n          </Button>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {error && (\\n        <Alert variant=\\"danger\\" dismissible onClose={() => setError(null)}>\\n          {error}\\n        </Alert>\\n      )}\\n\\n      {autoApplyEnabled && (\\n        <Alert variant=\\"danger\\" className=\\"d-flex align-items-center\\">\\n          <strong className=\\"me-2\\">BUMPERS OFF MODE ACTIVE</strong>\\n          <span>\\n            Recommendations will be automatically applied when you run analysis.\\n            Agent definitions will be modified without approval.\\n          </span>\\n        </Alert>\\n      )}\\n\\n      {/* Status Cards */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'secondary\'} text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Auto-Apply\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{autoApplyEnabled ? \'BUMPERS OFF\' : \'Manual\'}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg={status?.status === \'active\' ? \'success\' : \'secondary\'} text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Loop Status\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{status?.status || \'Unknown\'}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"info\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Feedback\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{status?.feedback_injection || \'N/A\'}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Pending\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{status?.pending_recommendations || 0}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"primary\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Approved\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{status?.approved_recommendations || 0}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n        <Col md={2}>\\n          <Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n            <Card.Body className=\\"py-2\\">\\n              <h6 className=\\"text-uppercase mb-1\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.7rem\', opacity: 0.8 }}>\\n                Applied\\n              </h6>\\n              <h4 className=\\"mb-0\\">{analysis?.auto_apply_results?.applied || 0}</h4>\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Analysis Results */}\\n      {analysis && (\\n        <Row className=\\"mb-4\\">\\n          <Col>\\n            <Card>\\n              <Card.Header>\\n                <strong>Latest Analysis Results</strong>\\n                <small className=\\"text-muted ms-2\\">\\n                  {new Date(analysis.analysis_timestamp).toLocaleString()}\\n                </small>\\n              </Card.Header>\\n              <Card.Body>\\n                <Row>\\n                  <Col md={4}>\\n                    <h6>Summary</h6>\\n                    <ul className=\\"list-unstyled\\">\\n                      <li>Period: Last {analysis.period_days} days</li>\\n                      <li>Recommendations: {analysis.recommendations_count}</li>\\n                      <li>\\n                        Critical Issues:{\' \'}\\n                        <Badge bg={analysis.critical_issues > 0 ? \'danger\' : \'success\'}>\\n                          {analysis.critical_issues}\\n                        </Badge>\\n                      </li>\\n                    </ul>\\n                  </Col>\\n                  <Col md={4}>\\n                    <h6>Common Issues Found</h6>\\n                    {Object.entries(analysis.patterns_found?.common_issues || {}).length > 0 ? (\\n                      <ul className=\\"list-unstyled\\">\\n                        {Object.entries(analysis.patterns_found.common_issues)\\n                          .sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])\\n                          .slice(0, 5)\\n                          .map(([issue, count]) => (\\n                            <li key={issue}>\\n                              <code>{issue}</code>: {count} occurrences\\n                            </li>\\n                          ))}\\n                      </ul>\\n                    ) : (\\n                      <p className=\\"text-muted\\">No patterns detected</p>\\n                    )}\\n                  </Col>\\n                  <Col md={4}>\\n                    <h6>Model Recommendations</h6>\\n                    {analysis.model_recommendations?.length > 0 ? (\\n                      <ul className=\\"list-unstyled\\">\\n                        {analysis.model_recommendations.map((rec, idx) => (\\n                          <li key={idx}>\\n                            <strong>{rec.agent}</strong>: Use {rec.recommend_model}\\n                            <br />\\n                            <small className=\\"text-success\\">{rec.improvement}</small>\\n                          </li>\\n                        ))}\\n                      </ul>\\n                    ) : (\\n                      <p className=\\"text-muted\\">No model optimizations suggested</p>\\n                    )}\\n                  </Col>\\n                </Row>\\n              </Card.Body>\\n            </Card>\\n          </Col>\\n        </Row>\\n      )}\\n\\n      {/* Pending Recommendations */}\\n      <Row>\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card>\\n            <Card.Header>\\n              <strong>Pending Recommendations</strong>\\n              <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\" className=\\"ms-2\\">\\n                {recommendations.length} pending\\n              </Badge>\\n            </Card.Header>\\n            <Card.Body style={{ maxHeight: \'500px\', overflowY: \'auto\' }}>\\n              {recommendations.length === 0 ? (\\n                <div className=\\"text-center py-4 text-muted\\">\\n                  <p>No pending recommendations.</p>\\n                  <p>Click \\"Run Analysis\\" to analyze agent performance and generate recommendations.</p>\\n                </div>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Table hover size=\\"sm\\">\\n                  <thead>\\n                    <tr>\\n                      <th>Priority</th>\\n                      <th>Agent</th>\\n                      <th>Type</th>\\n                      <th>Title</th>\\n                      <th>Actions</th>\\n                    </tr>\\n                  </thead>\\n                  <tbody>\\n                    {recommendations.map((rec) => (\\n                      <tr key={rec.id}>\\n                        <td>{getPriorityBadge(rec.priority)}</td>\\n                        <td><code>{rec.agent_name}</code></td>\\n                        <td>{getTypeBadge(rec.type)}</td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <strong>{rec.title}</strong>\\n                          <br />\\n                          <small className=\\"text-muted\\">{rec.description}</small>\\n                        </td>\\n                        <td>\\n                          <Button\\n                            variant=\\"warning\\"\\n                            size=\\"sm\\"\\n                            className=\\"me-1\\"\\n                            onClick={() => handleApplySingle(rec.id)}\\n                            title=\\"Approve AND apply changes to agent definition\\"\\n                          >\\n                            Apply\\n                          </Button>\\n                          <Button\\n                            variant=\\"outline-success\\"\\n                            size=\\"sm\\"\\n                            className=\\"me-1\\"\\n                            onClick={() => handleApprove(rec.id)}\\n                            title=\\"Approve without applying\\"\\n                          >\\n                            Approve\\n                          </Button>\\n                          <Button\\n                            variant=\\"outline-danger\\"\\n                            size=\\"sm\\"\\n                            onClick={() => openRejectModal(rec)}\\n                          >\\n                            Reject\\n                          </Button>\\n                        </td>\\n                      </tr>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </tbody>\\n                </Table>\\n              )}\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* How It Works */}\\n      <Row className=\\"mt-4 mb-4\\">\\n        <Col>\\n          <Card bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}>\\n            <Card.Body>\\n              <h6>How the Self-Improvement Loop Works {autoApplyEnabled && \'(BUMPERS OFF)\'}</h6>\\n              <ol className=\\"mb-0\\" style={{ fontSize: \'0.875rem\' }}>\\n                <li><strong>Collection:</strong> Every agent execution records metrics (success rate, duration, errors, self-analysis)</li>\\n                <li><strong>Analysis:</strong> The system periodically analyzes metrics to identify underperforming agents</li>\\n                <li><strong>Recommendations:</strong> Specific improvement suggestions are generated (model changes, definition tweaks)</li>\\n                {autoApplyEnabled ? (\\n                  <li><strong>Auto-Apply:</strong> <Badge bg=\\"warning\\" text=\\"dark\\">AUTOMATIC</Badge> Changes are immediately applied to agent definitions without human review</li>\\n                ) : (\\n                  <li><strong>Human Review:</strong> You approve or reject recommendations before they\'re applied</li>\\n                )}\\n                <li><strong>Feedback Injection:</strong> Insights are automatically included in agent prompts</li>\\n                <li><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> The loop repeats, tracking whether changes improve performance</li>\\n              </ol>\\n              {autoApplyEnabled && (\\n                <div className=\\"mt-3 p-2 bg-dark rounded\\">\\n                  <strong>Warning:</strong> In Bumpers Off mode, agent definitions (.md files) will be automatically modified.\\n                  Backups are created before changes. Toggle off to restore human-in-the-loop approval.\\n                </div>\\n              )}\\n            </Card.Body>\\n          </Card>\\n        </Col>\\n      </Row>\\n\\n      {/* Reject Modal */}\\n      <Modal show={showRejectModal} onHide={() => setShowRejectModal(false)}>\\n        <Modal.Header closeButton>\\n          <Modal.Title>Reject Recommendation</Modal.Title>\\n        </Modal.Header>\\n        <Modal.Body>\\n          {selectedRec && (\\n            <>\\n              <p><strong>Agent:</strong> {selectedRec.agent_name}</p>\\n              <p><strong>Title:</strong> {selectedRec.title}</p>\\n              <Form.Group>\\n                <Form.Label>Reason for rejection (optional)</Form.Label>\\n                <Form.Control\\n                  as=\\"textarea\\"\\n                  rows={3}\\n                  value={rejectReason}\\n                  onChange={(e) => setRejectReason(e.target.value)}\\n                  placeholder=\\"Why is this recommendation being rejected?\\"\\n                />\\n              </Form.Group>\\n            </>\\n          )}\\n        </Modal.Body>\\n        <Modal.Footer>\\n          <Button variant=\\"secondary\\" onClick={() => setShowRejectModal(false)}>\\n            Cancel\\n          </Button>\\n          <Button variant=\\"danger\\" onClick={handleReject}>\\n            Reject Recommendation\\n          </Button>\\n        </Modal.Footer>\\n      </Modal>\\n    </Container>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport default SelfImprovementDashboard;\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01561YUZBEfrY6vHyX4Gp6Lt', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'testers/unit_test_lead', 'input_data': {'task': 'Create accessibility and contrast tests for SelfImprovementDashboard component to identify readability issues', 'test_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx', 'code_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx', 'requirements': "Create comprehensive tests to validate: 1) Text contrast ratios meet WCAG 4.5:1 minimum, 2) No dark text on dark backgrounds, 3) All Bootstrap bg/text class combinations are correct, 4) Card components with bg='dark' have text='white', 5) Auto-apply toggle text visibility, 6) Badge readability, 7) Table content visibility, 8) Modal text readability. Tests should render component in different states and check computed styles.", 'test_type': 'accessibility_contrast', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01561YUZBEfrY6vHyX4Gp6Lt', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M1Sq78o9tRUwb1QJCWvpm2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M1Sq78o9tRUwb1QJCWvpm2', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.test.jsx"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'des