{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:59:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8ed73601-ab70-4ac6-890e-092b0f682808', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 2: Implementation and Testing - Fix text contrast issues and ensure readability across all elements",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BPQrvjHPhjtQqWo85XLxte', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BPQrvjHPhjtQqWo85XLxte', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: British Brass Band Achievements\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis project extends the existing Ensemble achievements system by adding a new \\"BRASS_BAND\\" achievement category. This follows an **extension pattern** - adding new content to an existing, well-structured system without modifying core architecture.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Plugin/Extension pattern for achievement categories\\n**Approach Rationale**: The existing achievements system is well-designed with clear enum-based categories and a list-based achievement registry. We simply extend these existing structures.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Current Stack (Maintained)\\n- **Backend**: Python with typed dataclasses for Achievement models\\n- **Frontend**: React with Bootstrap for UI components\\n- **State Management**: Props-based filtering in React components\\n- **API**: Existing achievement endpoints (no changes needed)\\n\\n### No New Dependencies Required\\nThe existing stack fully supports this extension.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n**1. AchievementCategory Enum** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Has SKA and other categories\\n- **Change**: Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` enum value\\n\\n**2. ACHIEVEMENTS List** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`)\\n- **Current State**: Contains Achievement objects for existing categories\\n- **Change**: Add 15 new Achievement objects for BRASS_BAND category\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n**3. AchievementsDashboard** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`)\\n- **Filter Dropdown**: Add brass_band option with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n- **getCategoryBadge Function**: Handle brass_band category styling\\n- **Fun Facts Section**: Optionally add brass band trivia\\n\\n### Component Interaction Flow\\n```\\nUser selects \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n    \\u2193\\nAchievementsDashboard filters by category=\\"brass_band\\"\\n    \\u2193\\nAPI returns achievements with category BRASS_BAND\\n    \\u2193\\nUI displays brass band achievements with proper badges\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.py          # MODIFY: Add enum + 15 achievements\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # MODIFY: Add filter + badge\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement Object (Existing Pattern)\\n```python\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,  # NEW CATEGORY\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Achievement Definitions (15 Total)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Rarity | Points | Trigger Type |\\n|----|------|--------|--------|--------------|\\n| championship_section | Championship Section | LEGENDARY | 200 | total_executions >= 50 |\\n| silver_band | Silver Band | RARE | 50 | consecutive_successes >= 5 |\\n| principal_cornet | Principal Cornet | UNCOMMON | 30 | sub_agents_led >= 3 |\\n| adjudicator | The Adjudicator | RARE | 60 | test_evaluations >= 25 |\\n| test_piece | Test Piece Mastery | UNCOMMON | 25 | iterations_in_task > 10 |\\n| bandroom_practice | Bandroom Practice | COMMON | 15 | total_executions >= 10 |\\n| promotion | Section Promotion | EPIC | 100 | success_rate_improvement |\\n| brass_section_harmony | Brass Section Harmony | RARE | 45 | concurrent_completions |\\n| march_on_stage | March on Stage | COMMON | 10 | first_task_in_project |\\n| quick_march | Quick March | RARE | 40 | task_time < 10s |\\n| hymn_tune_encore | Hymn Tune Encore | UNCOMMON | 35 | recovery_from_failure |\\n| grand_shield | Grand Shield | EPIC | 120 | consecutive_successes >= 25 |\\n| fanfare | Fanfare | RARE | 55 | achievements_in_session >= 5 |\\n| youth_band_graduate | Youth Band Graduate | UNCOMMON | 20 | new_agent_first_10_tasks |\\n| national_finals | National Finals | LEGENDARY | 150 | project_completion |\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API Changes Required**\\n- Existing `/api/achievements` endpoint supports category filtering\\n- Frontend already handles dynamic category data\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Testing\\n1. Verify BRASS_BAND enum exists\\n2. Verify 15 achievements load without errors\\n3. Verify achievement triggering works\\n4. Run existing achievement test suite\\n\\n### Frontend Testing\\n1. Verify brass_band filter appears in dropdown\\n2. Verify filter functionality works\\n3. Verify badge displays correctly\\n4. Verify no console errors\\n\\n### Manual Verification\\n- Load AchievementsDashboard\\n- Select \\"Brass Band\\" filter\\n- Verify achievements display with correct icons/badges\\n- Verify at least one achievement can trigger\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend (achievements.py)\\n1. Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to AchievementCategory enum\\n2. Add 15 Achievement objects to ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. Verify file imports correctly\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend (AchievementsDashboard.jsx)\\n1. Add brass_band to category filter dropdown\\n2. Update getCategoryBadge function\\n3. Optionally add fun facts\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Integration Testing\\n1. Run existing tests\\n2. Manual verification\\n3. Commit changes\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Condition Compatibility\\n**Impact**: New trigger conditions might not work with existing tracker\\n**Mitigation**: Use only existing trigger condition types\\n\\n### Risk 2: Frontend Filter Inconsistency\\n**Impact**: Filter might not match backend category name\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure exact string match \\"brass_band\\"\\n\\n## Key Implementation Decisions\\n\\n1. **Enum Value**: Use `brass_band` (lowercase with underscore) matching existing pattern\\n2. **Icon**: Use \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary icon since cornet emoji unavailable\\n3. **Trigger Conditions**: Reuse existing types, no new event tracking\\n4. **Points Range**: Follow existing scale based on rarity\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. \\u2705 BRASS_BAND in AchievementCategory enum\\n2. \\u2705 15 achievements in ACHIEVEMENTS list\\n3. \\u2705 brass_band filter works in UI\\n4. \\u2705 getCategoryBadge handles brass_band\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests pass\\n6. \\u2705 No console errors in frontend\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019t8hT1treCyR2auMD8TgFe', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019t8hT1treCyR2auMD8TgFe', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Vision**: Fix the unreadable text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) where black text appears on dark backgrounds, making it nearly impossible to read.\\n\\n**Problem**: Users report that the Improve page has severe readability issues with black text on dark backgrounds, creating a poor user experience and making the interface unusable in some areas.\\n\\n**Solution**: Identify and fix all instances of poor contrast between text and background colors to ensure proper readability across all UI elements.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Core Requirements\\n1. **Readability Fix**: Ensure all text on the Improve page is readable with proper contrast\\n2. **Bootstrap Consistency**: Maintain Bootstrap theme consistency while fixing contrast issues\\n3. **Dark Mode Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work properly in both light and dark mode contexts\\n4. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG guidelines for text contrast (minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text)\\n\\n### Specific Issues to Address\\n1. **Card Backgrounds**: Review all Card components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` and ensure text is white/light\\n2. **Alert Styling**: Ensure Alert components have proper text contrast\\n3. **Badge Colors**: Verify Badge components maintain readability\\n4. **Auto-Apply Toggle**: Check styling of the toggle switch and associated text\\n5. **Table Content**: Ensure table text is readable against backgrounds\\n6. **Modal Content**: Verify modal text readability\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Cannot break existing functionality\\n- Must preserve current color scheme intent (danger/warning/success indicators)\\n- Should use Bootstrap\'s built-in text color classes where possible\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page is readable with adequate contrast\\n2. No functionality is broken by the styling changes\\n3. Design maintains visual hierarchy and color-coded meanings\\n4. Changes are minimal and focused on contrast fixes only\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to other pages\\n- Functionality modifications\\n- Theme system overhaul\\n\\n## Analysis of Current Issues\\nBased on the SelfImprovementDashboard code review, potential problem areas:\\n\\n1. **Lines 266-267**: `bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\"` - This should be correct\\n2. **Lines 433-434**: Card with conditional background (`bg={autoApplyEnabled ? \'danger\' : \'light\'} text={autoApplyEnabled ? \'white\' : \'dark\'}`) - Light background with dark text should be readable\\n3. **Lines 451**: `bg-dark` class usage in auto-apply warning section\\n\\nThe issue might be in CSS overrides or Bootstrap theme customization that\'s causing text to appear black on dark backgrounds despite proper Bootstrap classes being used.\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- User is referring to the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page)\\n- Issue is with CSS/styling, not functional behavior\\n- Bootstrap framework is being used correctly in most places\\n- Problem may be in CSS overrides or theme customization\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n1. Analyze current styling and identify specific contrast violations\\n2. Fix styling issues using appropriate Bootstrap classes or custom CSS\\n3. Test readability across different states (auto-apply on/off, different card states)\\n4. Ensure accessibility compliance\\n5. Verify no regressions in functionality or other visual elements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011UuL7V2dPbCT3nuvDqZJXY', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Milestone 2: Text Contrast and Readability Fixes\n\n## Overview\nFix text contrast issues on the SelfImprovementDashboard component (Improve page) to ensure proper readability and WCAG compliance across all UI elements.\n\n## User Flows Affected\n1. **Primary Flow**: User navigating to Improve page\n   - User clicks "Improve" navigation\n   - Page loads with readable text on all elements\n   - User can interact with auto-apply toggle, cards, and modals\n2. **Secondary Flow**: User interacting with improvement suggestions\n   - User views improvement cards with clear, readable content\n   - User toggles auto-apply setting with visible feedback\n   - User dismisses suggestions with readable confirmation\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Task 1: Audit Current Contrast Issues\n**Type**: Analysis Task\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Description**: Systematically identify all text/background contrast violations on the SelfImprovementDashboard component.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All text elements analyzed for contrast ratio\n- [ ] Specific problem areas documented with line numbers\n- [ ] WCAG contrast requirements (4.5:1) validation completed\n- [ ] Both light and dark mode scenarios covered\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Files to Examine**:\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx`\n- Associated CSS files for theme overrides\n\n### Task 2: Fix Card Component Text Contrast\n**Type**: Styling Fix\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Ensure all Card components have proper text/background contrast ratios.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Cards with `bg="dark"` properly use `text="white"` or equivalent light text\n- [ ] Auto-apply toggle card maintains readability in both enabled/disabled states\n- [ ] Improvement suggestion cards have readable text\n- [ ] No visual regressions in card design hierarchy\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Key Areas**:\n- Auto-apply warning section (around line 451)\n- Dark background cards (lines 266-267)\n- Conditional background cards (lines 433-434)\n\n### Task 3: Fix Alert and Badge Components\n**Type**: Styling Fix  \n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Description**: Ensure Alert and Badge components maintain proper contrast across all states.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All Alert variants (danger, warning, info, success) have readable text\n- [ ] Badge components maintain contrast with parent backgrounds\n- [ ] Status indicators remain color-coded while being readable\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Components to Review**:\n- Bootstrap Alert components\n- Badge elements for status/priority indicators\n- Contextual color classes\n\n### Task 4: Fix Form and Interactive Element Contrast\n**Type**: Styling Fix\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Description**: Ensure form elements, toggles, and interactive components have proper contrast.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Auto-apply toggle switch is clearly visible\n- [ ] Toggle labels and descriptions are readable\n- [ ] Form validation text has adequate contrast\n- [ ] Interactive elements show clear focus states\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Focus Areas**:\n- Auto-apply toggle component\n- Form labels and help text\n- Button states and focus indicators\n\n### Task 5: Fix Table and List Content\n**Type**: Styling Fix\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Ensure table rows, list items, and structured content maintain readability.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Table headers and cells have proper contrast\n- [ ] Alternating row colors (if any) maintain readability\n- [ ] List items and nested content are clearly readable\n- [ ] Hover and selection states maintain contrast\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Areas to Check**:\n- Data tables for improvement metrics\n- Lists of suggestions or recommendations\n- Structured content displays\n\n### Task 6: Fix Modal and Overlay Content\n**Type**: Styling Fix\n**Complexity**: Simple  \n**Description**: Ensure modal dialogs and overlays have proper text contrast.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Modal headers, bodies, and footers are readable\n- [ ] Overlay text maintains contrast with backdrop\n- [ ] Modal close buttons and actions are clearly visible\n- [ ] Confirmation dialogs have adequate contrast\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Components**:\n- Improvement detail modals\n- Confirmation dialogs\n- Tooltip overlays\n\n### Task 7: CSS Theme Override Analysis\n**Type**: Technical Investigation\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Investigate and fix any CSS theme overrides causing contrast issues.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Custom CSS overrides identified and documented\n- [ ] Theme-level contrast issues resolved\n- [ ] Bootstrap class effectiveness verified\n- [ ] Global styling conflicts eliminated\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 completion\n**Investigation Areas**:\n- Custom CSS files\n- Bootstrap theme customizations\n- CSS-in-JS overrides\n- Global style conflicts\n\n### Task 8: Cross-State Testing and Validation\n**Type**: Quality Assurance\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Description**: Test contrast fixes across all component states and user scenarios.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All contrast issues resolved and verified\n- [ ] Auto-apply enabled/disabled states both readable\n- [ ] No functional regressions introduced\n- [ ] WCAG 2.1 AA compliance achieved (4.5:1 contrast ratio minimum)\n- [ ] Cross-browser compatibility maintained\n\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 2-7 completion\n**Test Scenarios**:\n- Auto-apply toggle on/off states\n- Different types of improvement suggestions\n- Modal interactions\n- Form validation states\n- Hover and focus states\n\n## Component Hierarchy\n```\nSelfImprovementDashboard (main component)\n├── Navigation elements\n├── Auto-apply toggle section\n│   ├── Card (conditional bg: danger/light)\n│   └── Toggle component with labels\n├── Improvement suggestions\n│   ├── Card components (potentially bg="dark")\n│   ├── Alert components\n│   └── Badge elements\n├── Data tables/lists\n└── Modal dialogs\n```\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. **Analysis First**: Systematically audit all text/background combinations\n2. **Bootstrap Classes**: Use built-in Bootstrap text classes (`text-white`, `text-dark`, etc.)\n3. **Minimal Changes**: Focus only on contrast fixes, preserve existing functionality\n4. **Testing**: Validate contrast ratios using WCAG tools\n5. **Documentation**: Document all changes for future maintenance\n\n## Dependencies Between Tasks\n- Task 1 (Audit) must complete before all other tasks\n- Tasks 2-7 can run in parallel after Task 1\n- Task 8 (Testing) requires Tasks 2-7 completion\n\n## Estimated Total Effort\n- **Analysis and Planning**: 2 hours\n- **Implementation**: 6-8 hours  \n- **Testing and Validation**: 2-3 hours\n- **Total**: 10-13 hours\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Zero contrast violations on WCAG evaluation\n- All text readable in both light/dark contexts\n- No functional regressions\n- User feedback confirms readability improvement'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011UuL7V2dPbCT3nuvDqZJXY', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2_20260114_215940.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2_20260114_215940.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.2\n- Common errors to a