"milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012Cv8i4zXT7FbxDrYW1LHdx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012Cv8i4zXT7FbxDrYW1LHdx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features & Enhancements\\n\\n## Development Workflow Improvements\\n\\n### 1. Frequent Coherent Commits (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Agents automatically commit work at logical checkpoints\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Clear audit trail of what each agent did\\n- Easy rollback if something goes wrong\\n- Better collaboration across agents\\n- Visibility into progress\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Add `git_commit` tool to agent toolkit\\n- Configure agents to commit after completing each task\\n- Commit message format: `[AgentName] TaskDescription\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: AgentName <agent@ensemble.ai>`\\n- Automatic staging of related files\\n\\n**Example**:\\n```python\\n# After Backend Developer writes code\\ngit_commit(\\n    message=\\"Implement user authentication endpoint\\",\\n    files=[\\"backend/auth.py\\", \\"backend/models/user.py\\"],\\n    agent_name=\\"Backend Developer\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Branch-Based Development System (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Each milestone/feature gets its own branch, agents work in parallel\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Simultaneous agent collaboration without conflicts\\n- Clean main branch (only merged\\u5b8c\\u6210 work)\\n- Easy code review before merging\\n- Supports multiple milestones in flight\\n\\n**Implementation Strategy**:\\n```\\nmain (stable, always deployable)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-0-foundation (Milestone 0 work)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-1-backend (Milestone 1 work)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-2-frontend (Milestone 2 work)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 feature/user-auth (specific feature branch)\\n```\\n\\n**Workflow**:\\n1. Executive Director creates branch: `git checkout -b milestone-X-name`\\n2. All agents work on that branch\\n3. Agents commit frequently to branch\\n4. When milestone complete, create PR to main\\n5. User reviews PR, merges when ready\\n\\n**Required Changes**:\\n- Add `git_branch` tool (create, switch branches)\\n- Add `git_merge` tool (merge branches)\\n- Add branch parameter to Executive Director input\\n- Update commit strategy to respect branches\\n\\n### 3. Concurrent Agent Sessions (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Multiple agent pipelines running simultaneously on different branches\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Parallel development of multiple features\\n- Faster overall delivery\\n- Better resource utilization\\n\\n**Example**:\\n```bash\\n# Terminal 1\\npython milestone_1_pipeline.py  # Working on backend\\n\\n# Terminal 2\\npython milestone_2_pipeline.py  # Working on frontend\\n\\n# Both can run simultaneously on different branches\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Agent Collaboration Protocol (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Agents can communicate/coordinate across branches\\n**Use Case**: Frontend agent needs to know if backend API is ready\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Shared state file (collaboration_state.json)\\n- Agents can publish \\"API ready\\" events\\n- Other agents can subscribe to events\\n- Cross-branch status checks\\n\\n## Code Quality & Testing\\n\\n### 5. Automated Code Review Agent (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Review code before committing, suggest improvements\\n**Checks**:\\n- Code style violations\\n- Security vulnerabilities\\n- Performance issues\\n- Test coverage gaps\\n\\n### 6. Continuous Integration Agent (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Run tests/linting on every commit\\n**Actions**:\\n- Run pytest automatically\\n- Run mypy type checking\\n- Run ruff linting\\n- Report failures to parent agent\\n- Block merge if tests fail\\n\\n### 7. Documentation Generator Agent (LOW PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Automatically generate/update documentation\\n**Generates**:\\n- API docs from code\\n- README updates\\n- Architecture diagrams\\n- Changelog from commits\\n\\n## Cost & Performance\\n\\n### 8. Cost Tracking & Budgeting (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Track API costs per agent\\n- Track API costs per milestone\\n- Alert when approaching budget limit\\n- Cost estimation before starting milestone\\n- Monthly/weekly cost reports\\n\\n### 9. Performance Metrics Dashboard (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Metrics**:\\n- Agent success rate\\n- Average iterations per agent\\n- Time to complete tasks\\n- API call efficiency\\n- Test coverage trends\\n\\n### 10. Agent Performance Learning (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: System learns which agents perform best for which tasks\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Track agent performance metrics\\n- Adjust model selection based on past performance\\n- Recommend agent consolidations based on redundancy\\n- Auto-tune max_iterations based on historical data\\n\\n## User Experience\\n\\n### 11. Interactive Web Dashboard (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Live agent execution visualization\\n- Click to see agent reasoning\\n- Manual intervention capability\\n- Cost tracking in real-time\\n- Branch/PR management\\n\\n### 12. Slack/Discord Integration (LOW PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Post milestone completions to Slack\\n- Alert on failures\\n- Command bot: `/ensemble status`, `/ensemble start milestone-3`\\n\\n### 13. Voice Interface (FUTURE)\\n**Concept**: \\"Ensemble, build me a REST API for task management\\"\\n**Status**: Far future, requires multimodal integration\\n\\n## Advanced Agent Features\\n\\n### 14. Self-Healing Agents (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: Agents detect their own failures and retry with different strategies\\n**Example**:\\n- Agent fails with haiku \\u2192 automatically retries with sonnet\\n- Test fails \\u2192 agent analyzes error, fixes bug, retries\\n- Spawn fails \\u2192 agent tries alternative agent or approach\\n\\n### 15. Agent Composition Engine (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: System automatically determines which agents needed for task\\n**Input**: \\"Build user authentication\\"\\n**Output**: Auto-composes pipeline:\\n- System Architect (design)\\n- Backend Developer (API)\\n- Frontend Developer (login form)\\n- Integration Test Writer (E2E tests)\\n\\n### 16. Multi-Provider LLM Routing (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Use different LLM providers based on task\\n**Example**:\\n- Anthropic Claude for strategic decisions\\n- OpenAI GPT-4 for creative writing\\n- Google Gemini for multimodal tasks\\n- Local Llama for simple tasks (cost savings)\\n\\n### 17. Knowledge Repository Agent (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Dedicated agent responsible for maintaining project context, architecture documentation, and responding to knowledge queries\\n**Role**:\\n- Maintains centralized knowledge base of project architecture\\n- Understands and documents design decisions\\n- Answers questions from other agents about project structure\\n- Tracks dependencies and relationships between components\\n- Maintains architectural decision records (ADRs)\\n\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Continuous project context throughout development lifecycle\\n- Reduces redundant architectural questions\\n- Improves consistency across agent decisions\\n- Single source of truth for \\"why\\" questions\\n- Better onboarding for new agents/humans joining project\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Persistent vector database for documentation embeddings\\n- Integration with code analysis tools\\n- Automatic ADR generation from architectural decisions\\n- Query interface for other agents via `knowledge_query` tool\\n- Regular sync with codebase to update context\\n\\n**Example Workflow**:\\n```python\\n# Backend Developer asks knowledge agent before implementing\\nresponse = knowledge_query(\\n    \\"What authentication pattern are we using for API endpoints?\\"\\n)\\n# Knowledge Agent responds with: \\"JWT-based auth, see auth/middleware.py and ADR-003\\"\\n\\n# After architectural decision, update knowledge base\\nrecord_decision(\\n    topic=\\"API Authentication\\",\\n    decision=\\"Use JWT with refresh tokens\\",\\n    rationale=\\"Better security, stateless, scales horizontally\\",\\n    alternatives_considered=[\\"Session-based\\", \\"OAuth2\\"],\\n    file_path=\\"docs/architecture/ADR-003-api-auth.md\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## Infrastructure\\n\\n### 18. Docker-Based Agent Execution (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Isolated environments per agent\\n- Reproducible builds\\n- Easy deployment\\n- Security isolation\\n\\n### 19. Distributed Agent Execution (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: Run agents on different machines/cloud instances\\n**Benefits**:\\n- True parallelization\\n- Scale to many simultaneous agents\\n- Fault tolerance\\n\\n### 20. State Persistence & Recovery (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Save pipeline state every N iterations\\n- Resume from last checkpoint on failure\\n- Export/import session state\\n- Replay past sessions\\n\\n## Security & Compliance\\n\\n### 21. Secrets Management (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Agents never see raw API keys\\n- Secrets stored in secure vault\\n- Audit log of secret access\\n- Rotation of credentials\\n\\n### 22. Audit Trail (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Track**:\\n- Every file written\\n- Every command executed\\n- Every API call made\\n- Cost per action\\n- Agent decision reasoning\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1 (Milestone 0-1)**: Foundation\\n- \\u2705 Agent consolidation\\n- \\u2705 Drum corps cleanup\\n- [ ] Frequent commits (auto-commit tool)\\n- [ ] Branch-based development\\n- [ ] State persistence\\n\\n**Phase 2 (Milestone 2-3)**: Quality & Visibility\\n- [ ] Automated CI agent\\n- [ ] Cost tracking\\n- [ ] Performance metrics\\n- [ ] Code review agent\\n\\n**Phase 3 (Milestone 4+)**: Advanced Features\\n- [ ] Agent performance learning\\n- [ ] Multi-provider routing\\n- [ ] Web dashboard\\n- [ ] Agent composition engine\\n\\n**Phase 4 (Future)**: Innovation\\n- [ ] Self-healing agents\\n- [ ] Distributed execution\\n- [ ] Voice interface\\n- [ ] Advanced collaboration\\n\\n## Notes\\n- Features marked HIGH PRIORITY should be in next 2-3 milestones\\n- MEDIUM PRIORITY features can wait until system is stable\\n- ADVANCED features require significant R&D\\n- Get user feedback before implementing FUTURE features\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PqwXnQo36kK1xh3METxNuv', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'c7dc6764', 'category': 'decision', 'note': 'Analyzed FUTURE_FEATURES.md document - contains 22 major features/enhancements spanning development workflow, code quality, cost tracking, UX improvements, advanced agent features, and infrastructure. Document includes clear prioritization (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/ADVANCED) and phases. Will focus on implementing highest priority items first: frequent commits, branch-based development, CI agent, cost tracking, knowledge repository, and state persistence.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PqwXnQo36kK1xh3METxNuv', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VrHSYTts2hwMz4BnRE5nTe', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Future Features Implementation Requirements\n\n## Vision\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\n\n## Objectives\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\n\n## Scope\n\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\n\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\n\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\n\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\n\n## Target Users\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\n\n## Constraints\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\n\n## Technical Requirements\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\n- Mobile application interface\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\n- Frequent commits system\n- Branch-based development\n- State persistence\n- Secrets management\n\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \n- CI/CD agent\n- Cost tracking\n- Performance metrics\n- Code review automation\n\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\n- Knowledge repository agent\n- Agent performance learning\n- Multi-provider routing\n- Self-healing capabilities\n\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\n- Web dashboard\n- Integration capabilities\n- Advanced collaboration features\n\n## Assumptions Made\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\n\n## Dependencies\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VrHSYTts2hwMz4BnRE5nTe', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_231347.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_231347.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014ZGK2jXMtcn8yU32Xb91Jz', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'c7dc6764', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements documentation completed. Analyzed 22 features from FUTURE_FEATURES.md and created comprehensive requirements document with clear prioritization: 7 HIGH priority features for immediate implementation, 7 MEDIUM priority for phase 2, 4 ADVANCED for phase 3, and 4 FUTURE features. Document includes success criteria, constraints, technical requirements, and risk mitigation strategies.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014ZGK2jXMtcn8yU32Xb91Jz', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Vp5RfnXvjyMhD5L4j2zYdG', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'c7dc6764', 'description': 'Orchestrate implementation of all 22 features from FUTURE_FEATURES.md through coordinated multi-agent development system', 'assigned_to': 'leadership/development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Vp5RfnXvjyMhD5L4j2zYdG', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "d7b80606", "message": "Added task: Orchestrate implementation of all 22 features from FUTURE_FEATURES.md through coordinated multi-agent development system"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 85.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 16.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed well in this execution by: 1) Quickly recognizing this was an expansion of an existing system rather than new development, 2) Conducting thorough research into the current achievement syst...\n- Performance Assessment: I successfully completed the requirements gathering phase by analyzing the user\'s clear request and creating a comprehensive requirements document. I followed protocol by creat...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
