{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:14:46", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c0e3e3fe-e5ca-41fe-bb6b-4556878fb4cb', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Future Features Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01T2qrHAtzRqo4EYk5DL8QPt', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01T2qrHAtzRqo4EYk5DL8QPt', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CnWfYsMxbCUQQgqWT4BAjU', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Future Features Implementation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nImplementing 22 comprehensive features for the Ensemble multi-agent development platform, focusing on development workflow, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 0: Foundation Infrastructure\n**Objective**: Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows and state management\n**Duration**: 2-3 weeks\n**Dependencies**: None (starting milestone)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Enhanced git tooling with proper commit formatting and agent attribution\n- Basic branch management system for milestone-based development\n- State persistence framework with checkpoint capabilities\n- Secrets management foundation with secure credential handling\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Git commits automatically formatted with agent attribution\n- Branch creation/switching for milestones works reliably\n- State can be saved and restored between agent sessions\n- API keys and credentials stored securely with audit logging\n- All changes tested and documented\n\n**Risk Factors**: \n- Git workflow complexity may require extensive testing\n- State persistence design needs careful architecture planning\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 1: Development Workflow Enhancement  \n**Objective**: Complete branch-based development system with agent collaboration\n**Duration**: 3-4 weeks\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 0 (git foundation, state persistence)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Complete branch-based development system with PR management\n- Concurrent agent session support on different branches\n- Agent collaboration protocol with cross-branch communication\n- Enhanced git conflict resolution and merge strategies\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Multiple agents can work on separate branches simultaneously\n- Agents can communicate status and coordinate work across branches\n- Merge conflicts handled gracefully with rollback capabilities\n- Branch management integrates seamlessly with existing workflows\n- Performance impact minimal compared to single-branch execution\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Concurrent execution complexity may introduce race conditions\n- Agent coordination protocols need thorough testing\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: Quality Assurance & CI/CD\n**Objective**: Implement automated quality assurance and continuous integration\n**Duration**: 3-4 weeks  \n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (branch-based development)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Continuous Integration Agent with automated testing and linting\n- Automated Code Review Agent for pre-commit quality analysis\n- Quality metrics collection and reporting\n- Integration with existing test frameworks\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All code changes automatically tested before merge\n- Code quality issues detected and flagged pre-commit\n- CI/CD pipeline integrates with branch-based workflow\n- Quality metrics tracked and reportable\n- Zero false positives in automated reviews (>95% accuracy)\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Code review accuracy may require fine-tuning\n- CI/CD integration complexity with existing toolchain\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 3: Cost Management & Performance Tracking\n**Objective**: Implement comprehensive cost tracking and performance monitoring\n**Duration**: 2-3 weeks\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 0 (state persistence for data storage)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Cost tracking system with API usage monitoring\n- Budget alerts and reporting dashboard\n- Performance metrics collection for all agents\n- Agent efficiency analysis and optimization recommendations\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Real-time cost tracking for all LLM API calls\n- Budget alerts trigger before overspend occurs\n- Performance metrics show agent success rates and efficiency\n- Historical data available for trend analysis\n- Cost attribution by project, milestone, and agent type\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- API cost calculation accuracy across multiple providers\n- Performance monitoring overhead on system resources\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 4: Knowledge Management & Intelligence\n**Objective**: Implement knowledge repository and intelligent agent features\n**Duration**: 4-5 weeks\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 0 (state persistence), Milestone 3 (performance data)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Knowledge Repository Agent with centralized project context\n- Agent Performance Learning system with historical optimization\n- Multi-Provider LLM Routing with task-based model selection\n- Architectural decision tracking and documentation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Knowledge repository maintains comprehensive project context\n- Agent assignments optimize based on historical performance data\n- LLM routing selects optimal models for specific task types\n- System learns and improves over time without manual intervention\n- Knowledge base searchable and maintains version history\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Machine learning model accuracy for agent assignment\n- Knowledge base design complexity for diverse project types\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 5: Self-Healing & Advanced Features\n**Objective**: Implement self-healing capabilities and advanced automation\n**Duration**: 3-4 weeks\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (performance learning), Milestone 2 (quality assurance)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Self-Healing Agents with automatic failure detection\n- Agent Composition Engine for automatic pipeline generation\n- Advanced error recovery and strategy adjustment\n- Audit trail system with comprehensive action logging\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- System automatically detects and recovers from agent failures\n- Pipeline generation adapts to different project requirements\n- Recovery strategies improve based on failure pattern analysis\n- Complete audit trail available for all agent actions\n- Self-healing success rate >90% for common failure patterns\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Self-healing complexity may introduce unexpected behaviors\n- Automatic pipeline generation accuracy for diverse project types\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 6: User Experience & Visualization\n**Objective**: Create interactive dashboard and user interface improvements\n**Duration**: 4-5 weeks\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3 (performance metrics), Milestone 5 (audit trail)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Interactive Web Dashboard with live execution visualization\n- Manual intervention capabilities during agent execution\n- Real-time status monitoring and control interface\n- User-friendly configuration and management tools\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Dashboard provides real-time visibility into all agent activities\n- Users can intervene and redirect agent execution when needed\n- Interface is intuitive and requires minimal training\n- Dashboard performance acceptable with multiple concurrent sessions\n- Mobile-responsive design for remote monitoring\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Web interface complexity may require significant frontend development\n- Real-time updates may impact system performance\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 7: Integration & Documentation\n**Objective**: Complete integration capabilities and comprehensive documentation\n**Duration**: 2-3 weeks\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones (complete feature set)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Documentation Generator Agent with automated documentation\n- Slack/Discord integration for team communication\n- Docker-based agent execution environment\n- Complete user documentation and deployment guides\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Documentation automatically generated and maintained\n- Team integration platforms provide command interface and notifications\n- Containerized execution available for all agent types\n- Documentation comprehensive and user-tested\n- Deployment process streamlined and reliable\n\n**Risk Factors**:\n- Integration platform complexity across different team workflows\n- Documentation generator accuracy for technical content\n\n---\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n### Technical Resources:\n- Database for persistent storage (cost tracking, metrics, knowledge base)\n- Enhanced git integration with conflict resolution\n- Web framework for dashboard implementation  \n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution\n- Security infrastructure for secrets management\n\n### Development Resources:\n- Backend development (APIs, data persistence, agent coordination)\n- Frontend development (web dashboard, user interface)\n- DevOps/Infrastructure (CI/CD, containerization, deployment)\n- Testing/QA (automated testing, integration testing, performance testing)\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### Quantitative:\n- All 7 HIGH PRIORITY features implemented and tested\n- Zero regressions in existing functionality\n- >95% uptime for new services\n- <10% performance impact on existing workflows\n- 100% test coverage for new features\n\n### Qualitative:\n- User satisfaction with new capabilities\n- Reduced manual intervention in development workflows  \n- Improved agent coordination and efficiency\n- Enhanced visibility into system operations\n- Streamlined onboarding for new users\n\n## Risk Mitigation Strategy\n\n### High Risk Items:\n1. **Git workflow complexity** - Extensive testing, staged rollout, rollback procedures\n2. **Concurrent agent coordination** - Robust locking mechanisms, conflict resolution\n3. **Performance impact** - Continuous monitoring, resource limits, optimization\n\n### Medium Risk Items:\n1. **Integration complexity** - Phased implementation, component validation\n2. **User adoption** - Training materials, gradual feature rollout\n3. **Security vulnerabilities** - Security reviews, penetration testing\n\n## Delivery Timeline\n**Total Duration**: 20-28 weeks (5-7 months)\n**Critical Path**: Foundation → Development Workflow → Quality Assurance → Advanced Features\n**Parallel Tracks**: Cost Management can run parallel with Quality Assurance\n**Buffer Time**: 20% contingency built into each milestone for unexpected complexity\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Begin Milestone 0 implementation with enhanced git tooling\n2. Establish development environment for new features\n3. Set up monitoring and tracking for milestone progress\n4. Schedule regular stakeholder reviews and feedback sessions'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CnWfYsMxbCUQQgqWT4BAjU', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231442.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231442.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'r