{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:15:02", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-48b000af-041c-443a-94c3-90c686a1bc6a', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Frontend Fix Implementation - Implement CSS/styling fixes to resolve all text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KfCYSEpvnUufMkAaFu55K5', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KfCYSEpvnUufMkAaFu55K5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017fdaQf1amQRMSfRFGNGEPU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017fdaQf1amQRMSfRFGNGEPU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VBkEsx5DwhNDzHocYFaoan', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Frontend Fix Implementation\n\n## Milestone Overview\nFrontend Fix Implementation - Implement CSS/styling fixes to resolve all text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component\n\n## Test Strategy Summary\nThis milestone focuses on CSS/styling fixes for accessibility compliance (WCAG 2.1 AA standards). The testing strategy emphasizes visual regression testing, accessibility validation, and cross-browser compatibility to ensure the fixes resolve contrast issues without breaking existing functionality.\n\n## Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 90% (CSS styling logic, conditional class application)\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% (component rendering with different themes)\n- **E2E Coverage**: Critical user paths (normal mode, "bumpers off" mode)\n- **Visual Regression**: 100% (before/after screenshots for all styling states)\n- **Accessibility Coverage**: 100% WCAG 2.1 AA compliance verification\n\n## Test Types Required\n\n### 1. Unit Tests\n**Target**: CSS class generation logic, conditional styling functions\n**Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library\n**Coverage**: 90%\n\n### 2. Visual Regression Tests  \n**Target**: Component appearance in different modes\n**Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library (snapshot testing)\n**Coverage**: All visual states\n\n### 3. Accessibility Tests\n**Target**: WCAG 2.1 compliance verification\n**Framework**: jest-axe + manual validation\n**Coverage**: 100% color contrast compliance\n\n### 4. Integration Tests\n**Target**: Component behavior with theme switching\n**Framework**: React Testing Library\n**Coverage**: All theme combinations\n\n### 5. Cross-Browser Tests\n**Target**: Visual consistency across browsers\n**Framework**: Manual testing (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\n**Coverage**: Primary user flows\n\n## Test Task Breakdown\n\n### Task 1: Unit Tests for Styling Logic\n**Type**: Unit Test  \n**Priority**: High  \n**Estimated Effort**: 2 hours  \n**Framework**: Jest + React Testing Library\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Test conditional CSS class generation for normal mode\n- Test conditional CSS class generation for "bumpers off" mode  \n- Test color class selection logic for different background types\n- Test Bootstrap class combination logic\n- Test edge cases (undefined states, invalid inputs)\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- `SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx` - styling logic functions\n- Any utility functions for theme/color management\n\n### Task 2: Visual Regression Tests\n**Type**: Visual Regression  \n**Priority**: High  \n**Estimated Effort**: 3 hours  \n**Framework**: Jest snapshot testing\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Snapshot test: Dashboard in normal mode\n- Snapshot test: Dashboard in "bumpers off" mode\n- Snapshot test: Individual card components with different backgrounds\n- Snapshot test: Badge components in both themes\n- Snapshot test: Table elements with proper contrast\n- Snapshot test: Responsive breakpoints (mobile, tablet, desktop)\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- `SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx` - complete component rendering\n\n### Task 3: Accessibility Compliance Tests\n**Type**: Accessibility  \n**Priority**: Critical  \n**Estimated Effort**: 4 hours  \n**Framework**: jest-axe + manual validation\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratio testing (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text)\n- Color contrast validation for all text/background combinations\n- Focus management and keyboard navigation\n- Screen reader compatibility testing\n- Color-blind accessibility verification\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- `SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx` - all rendered text elements\n\n### Task 4: Theme Integration Tests\n**Type**: Integration  \n**Priority**: High  \n**Estimated Effort**: 2 hours  \n**Framework**: React Testing Library\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Test component rendering with normal theme state\n- Test component rendering with danger theme state\n- Test theme switching behavior (if applicable)\n- Test prop passing for theme-related data\n- Test component rerender behavior on theme changes\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- `SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx` - full component integration\n\n### Task 5: Cross-Browser Compatibility Tests\n**Type**: Manual/E2E  \n**Priority**: Medium  \n**Estimated Effort**: 3 hours  \n**Framework**: Manual testing + browser dev tools\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Chrome: Visual verification of all styling fixes\n- Firefox: Ensure CSS compatibility and rendering consistency\n- Safari: macOS-specific rendering validation\n- Edge: Windows compatibility verification\n- Mobile browsers: Responsive behavior validation\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- Complete application in browser environments\n\n### Task 6: Performance Impact Tests\n**Type**: Performance  \n**Priority**: Low  \n**Estimated Effort**: 1 hour  \n**Framework**: React DevTools Profiler\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Measure component render time before/after fixes\n- Verify no additional CSS bundle size impact  \n- Test for any memory leaks from styling changes\n- Validate smooth animations/transitions\n\n**Files to Test**:\n- `SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx` - performance characteristics\n\n## Test Environment Setup\n\n### Local Development\n```bash\nnpm test                    # Run unit tests\nnpm test -- --coverage     # Generate coverage report\nnpm test -- --watch        # Run tests in watch mode\n```\n\n### Browser Testing\n```bash\nnpm start                   # Start development server\n# Manual testing in multiple browsers\n```\n\n### Accessibility Testing\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev jest-axe\n# Additional manual testing with screen readers\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Unit Tests\n- [ ] 90%+ code coverage for styling logic\n- [ ] All conditional styling functions tested\n- [ ] Edge cases handled appropriately\n- [ ] No false positives in test assertions\n\n### Visual Regression\n- [ ] Snapshot tests capture all visual states\n- [ ] Screenshots validate contrast improvements\n- [ ] No unintended visual changes detected\n- [ ] Responsive design preserved\n\n### Accessibility\n- [ ] WCAG 2.1 AA compliance achieved (4.5:1 contrast)\n- [ ] All text readable in both normal and danger modes\n- [ ] No accessibility regressions introduced\n- [ ] Screen reader compatibility maintained\n\n### Integration\n- [ ] Component behavior consistent across theme states\n- [ ] No breaking changes to existing functionality\n- [ ] Props and state management working correctly\n- [ ] Performance impact negligible\n\n### Cross-Browser\n- [ ] Consistent appearance across Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n- [ ] Mobile responsiveness maintained\n- [ ] CSS compatibility verified\n- [ ] No browser-specific rendering issues\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### Risk: CSS Specificity Conflicts\n**Mitigation**: Use inline styles where needed, test in actual browser environment\n\n### Risk: Breaking Existing Visual Design\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive snapshot testing, before/after visual comparison\n\n### Risk: Accessibility Non-Compliance  \n**Mitigation**: Automated jest-axe testing + manual validation with accessibility tools\n\n### Risk: Performance Degradation\n**Mitigation**: Performance testing with React DevTools, bundle size analysis\n\n### Risk: Cross-Browser Inconsistencies\n**Mitigation**: Test in multiple browsers, use standard Bootstrap classes\n\n## Test Data Requirements\n\n### Mock Data\n- Component props for different dashboard states\n- Sample performance data for display testing\n- Various user permission states\n- Error state mock data\n\n### Test Fixtures\n- Theme configuration objects\n- CSS class mapping fixtures\n- Accessibility test scenarios\n- Browser compatibility matrices\n\n## Automation Strategy\n\n### Continuous Integration\n- Unit tests run on every commit\n- Accessibility tests in CI pipeline\n- Visual regression tests on PR creation\n- Coverage reports generated automatically\n\n### Manual Testing Checkpoints\n- Cross-browser testing before release\n- User acceptance testing for readability\n- Accessibility audit with real users\n- Performance validation in production-like environment\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Testing Dependencies\n- jest (existing)\n- @testing-library/react (existing)\n- jest-axe (to be added)\n- @testing-library/jest-dom (existing)\n\n### Development Dependencies\n- React DevTools (for performance testing)\n- Browser dev tools (for accessibility testing)\n- Multiple browser installations\n\n## Documentation Requirements\n\n### Test Documentation\n- Test case descriptions and rationale\n- Coverage reports with explanations\n- Accessibility compliance documentation\n- Cross-browser compatibility matrix\n- Performance impact analysis\n\n### User Documentation\n- Before/after screenshots showing improvements\n- Accessibility compliance statement\n- Browser support documentation\n- Known issues and workarounds (if any)\n\n---\n\n**Total Estimated Effort**: 15 hours\n**Total Test Tasks**: 6 tasks\n**Primary Focus**: Accessibility compliance and visual regression prevention\n**Success Metric**: 100% WCAG 2.1 AA compliance with no visual regressions'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VBkEsx5DwhNDzHocYFaoan', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2_20260114_231501.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2_20260114_231501.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
