{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:17:36", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2feae690-1428-4e49-a3e6-7bb165d0e6aa', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement **all tasks defined in** `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` end-to-end.\\n\\nYou are operating as a coordinated multi-agent system (Executive Director, Development Manager, System Architect, and implementation agents). Your goal is to fully deliver every feature, enhancement, and refactor described in that document.\\n\\n**Instructions:**\\n\\n1. **Read and interpret the document**\\n   - Parse every section, bullet, and task in `FUTURE_FEATURES.md`.\\n   - Treat all listed items as required scope unless explicitly marked optional.\\n\\n2. **Plan before execution**\\n   - Produce a clear implementation plan covering:\\n     - Feature breakdown\\n     - Dependencies and ordering\\n     - Required architectural changes\\n     - Risks and mitigation\\n   - Align with existing Ensemble architecture, conventions, and coding style.\\n\\n3. **Execute incrementally**\\n   - Implement features in logical milestones.\\n   - Prefer small, reviewable changes over monolithic commits.\\n   - Reuse existing abstractions where appropriate; refactor only when justified.\\n\\n4. **Code quality and standards**\\n   - Maintain consistency with the current codebase (naming, patterns, structure).\\n   - Write clean, well-factored, production-ready code.\\n   - Avoid speculative features not present in the document.\\n\\n5. **Validation**\\n   - Add or update tests where applicable.\\n   - Verify UI, agent behavior, and orchestration logic function as intended.\\n   - Ensure no regressions in existing functionality.\\n\\n6. **Documentation**\\n   - Update or create documentation for each implemented feature.\\n   - Clearly note any deviations or assumptions made during implementation.\\n\\n7. **Completion criteria**\\n   - Every task in `FUTURE_FEATURES.md` is implemented, tested, and documented.\\n   - The system builds and runs successfully.\\n   - All agents report completion with a concise summary of delivered work.\\n\\nBegin by reading the file, generating the execution plan, then proceed through implementation until the full document is complete.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SaKsbwt3Rn24YBUrf1ap4H', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Future Features Implementation', 'description': 'Implement all tasks defined in FUTURE_FEATURES.md end-to-end using coordinated multi-agent system'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SaKsbwt3Rn24YBUrf1ap4H', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "c7dc6764", "message": "Created project: Future Features Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "c7dc6764", "project_name": "Future Features Implementation", "description": "Implement all tasks defined in FUTURE_FEATURES.md end-to-end using coordinated multi-agent system", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-14T23:13:08.670362", "updated_at": "2026-01-14T23:13:08.670362", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-14T23:13:08.670362", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Future Features Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012Cv8i4zXT7FbxDrYW1LHdx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012Cv8i4zXT7FbxDrYW1LHdx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features & Enhancements\\n\\n## Development Workflow Improvements\\n\\n### 1. Frequent Coherent Commits (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Agents automatically commit work at logical checkpoints\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Clear audit trail of what each agent did\\n- Easy rollback if something goes wrong\\n- Better collaboration across agents\\n- Visibility into progress\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Add `git_commit` tool to agent toolkit\\n- Configure agents to commit after completing each task\\n- Commit message format: `[AgentName] TaskDescription\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: AgentName <agent@ensemble.ai>`\\n- Automatic staging of related files\\n\\n**Example**:\\n```python\\n# After Backend Developer writes code\\ngit_commit(\\n    message=\\"Implement user authentication endpoint\\",\\n    files=[\\"backend/auth.py\\", \\"backend/models/user.py\\"],\\n    agent_name=\\"Backend Developer\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Branch-Based Development System (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Each milestone/feature gets its own branch, agents work in parallel\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Simultaneous agent collaboration without conflicts\\n- Clean main branch (only merged\\u5b8c\\u6210 work)\\n- Easy code review before merging\\n- Supports multiple milestones in flight\\n\\n**Implementation Strategy**:\\n```\\nmain (stable, always deployable)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-0-foundation (Milestone 0 work)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-1-backend (Milestone 1 work)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone-2-frontend (Milestone 2 work)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 feature/user-auth (specific feature branch)\\n```\\n\\n**Workflow**:\\n1. Executive Director creates branch: `git checkout -b milestone-X-name`\\n2. All agents work on that branch\\n3. Agents commit frequently to branch\\n4. When milestone complete, create PR to main\\n5. User reviews PR, merges when ready\\n\\n**Required Changes**:\\n- Add `git_branch` tool (create, switch branches)\\n- Add `git_merge` tool (merge branches)\\n- Add branch parameter to Executive Director input\\n- Update commit strategy to respect branches\\n\\n### 3. Concurrent Agent Sessions (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Multiple agent pipelines running simultaneously on different branches\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Parallel development of multiple features\\n- Faster overall delivery\\n- Better resource utilization\\n\\n**Example**:\\n```bash\\n# Terminal 1\\npython milestone_1_pipeline.py  # Working on backend\\n\\n# Terminal 2\\npython milestone_2_pipeline.py  # Working on frontend\\n\\n# Both can run simultaneously on different branches\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Agent Collaboration Protocol (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Agents can communicate/coordinate across branches\\n**Use Case**: Frontend agent needs to know if backend API is ready\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Shared state file (collaboration_state.json)\\n- Agents can publish \\"API ready\\" events\\n- Other agents can subscribe to events\\n- Cross-branch status checks\\n\\n## Code Quality & Testing\\n\\n### 5. Automated Code Review Agent (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Review code before committing, suggest improvements\\n**Checks**:\\n- Code style violations\\n- Security vulnerabilities\\n- Performance issues\\n- Test coverage gaps\\n\\n### 6. Continuous Integration Agent (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Run tests/linting on every commit\\n**Actions**:\\n- Run pytest automatically\\n- Run mypy type checking\\n- Run ruff linting\\n- Report failures to parent agent\\n- Block merge if tests fail\\n\\n### 7. Documentation Generator Agent (LOW PRIORITY)\\n**Role**: Automatically generate/update documentation\\n**Generates**:\\n- API docs from code\\n- README updates\\n- Architecture diagrams\\n- Changelog from commits\\n\\n## Cost & Performance\\n\\n### 8. Cost Tracking & Budgeting (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Track API costs per agent\\n- Track API costs per milestone\\n- Alert when approaching budget limit\\n- Cost estimation before starting milestone\\n- Monthly/weekly cost reports\\n\\n### 9. Performance Metrics Dashboard (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Metrics**:\\n- Agent success rate\\n- Average iterations per agent\\n- Time to complete tasks\\n- API call efficiency\\n- Test coverage trends\\n\\n### 10. Agent Performance Learning (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: System learns which agents perform best for which tasks\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Track agent performance metrics\\n- Adjust model selection based on past performance\\n- Recommend agent consolidations based on redundancy\\n- Auto-tune max_iterations based on historical data\\n\\n## User Experience\\n\\n### 11. Interactive Web Dashboard (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Live agent execution visualization\\n- Click to see agent reasoning\\n- Manual intervention capability\\n- Cost tracking in real-time\\n- Branch/PR management\\n\\n### 12. Slack/Discord Integration (LOW PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Post milestone completions to Slack\\n- Alert on failures\\n- Command bot: `/ensemble status`, `/ensemble start milestone-3`\\n\\n### 13. Voice Interface (FUTURE)\\n**Concept**: \\"Ensemble, build me a REST API for task management\\"\\n**Status**: Far future, requires multimodal integration\\n\\n## Advanced Agent Features\\n\\n### 14. Self-Healing Agents (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: Agents detect their own failures and retry with different strategies\\n**Example**:\\n- Agent fails with haiku \\u2192 automatically retries with sonnet\\n- Test fails \\u2192 agent analyzes error, fixes bug, retries\\n- Spawn fails \\u2192 agent tries alternative agent or approach\\n\\n### 15. Agent Composition Engine (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: System automatically determines which agents needed for task\\n**Input**: \\"Build user authentication\\"\\n**Output**: Auto-composes pipeline:\\n- System Architect (design)\\n- Backend Developer (API)\\n- Frontend Developer (login form)\\n- Integration Test Writer (E2E tests)\\n\\n### 16. Multi-Provider LLM Routing (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Use different LLM providers based on task\\n**Example**:\\n- Anthropic Claude for strategic decisions\\n- OpenAI GPT-4 for creative writing\\n- Google Gemini for multimodal tasks\\n- Local Llama for simple tasks (cost savings)\\n\\n### 17. Knowledge Repository Agent (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Concept**: Dedicated agent responsible for maintaining project context, architecture documentation, and responding to knowledge queries\\n**Role**:\\n- Maintains centralized knowledge base of project architecture\\n- Understands and documents design decisions\\n- Answers questions from other agents about project structure\\n- Tracks dependencies and relationships between components\\n- Maintains architectural decision records (ADRs)\\n\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Continuous project context throughout development lifecycle\\n- Reduces redundant architectural questions\\n- Improves consistency across agent decisions\\n- Single source of truth for \\"why\\" questions\\n- Better onboarding for new agents/humans joining project\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Persistent vector database for documentation embeddings\\n- Integration with code analysis tools\\n- Automatic ADR generation from architectural decisions\\n- Query interface for other agents via `knowledge_query` tool\\n- Regular sync with codebase to update context\\n\\n**Example Workflow**:\\n```python\\n# Backend Developer asks knowledge agent before implementing\\nresponse = knowledge_query(\\n    \\"What authentication pattern are we using for API endpoints?\\"\\n)\\n# Knowledge Agent responds with: \\"JWT-based auth, see auth/middleware.py and ADR-003\\"\\n\\n# After architectural decision, update knowledge base\\nrecord_decision(\\n    topic=\\"API Authentication\\",\\n    decision=\\"Use JWT with refresh tokens\\",\\n    rationale=\\"Better security, stateless, scales horizontally\\",\\n    alternatives_considered=[\\"Session-based\\", \\"OAuth2\\"],\\n    file_path=\\"docs/architecture/ADR-003-api-auth.md\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## Infrastructure\\n\\n### 18. Docker-Based Agent Execution (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Benefits**:\\n- Isolated environments per agent\\n- Reproducible builds\\n- Easy deployment\\n- Security isolation\\n\\n### 19. Distributed Agent Execution (ADVANCED)\\n**Concept**: Run agents on different machines/cloud instances\\n**Benefits**:\\n- True parallelization\\n- Scale to many simultaneous agents\\n- Fault tolerance\\n\\n### 20. State Persistence & Recovery (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Save pipeline state every N iterations\\n- Resume from last checkpoint on failure\\n- Export/import session state\\n- Replay past sessions\\n\\n## Security & Compliance\\n\\n### 21. Secrets Management (HIGH PRIORITY)\\n**Features**:\\n- Agents never see raw API keys\\n- Secrets stored in secure vault\\n- Audit log of secret access\\n- Rotation of credentials\\n\\n### 22. Audit Trail (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\\n**Track**:\\n- Every file written\\n- Every command executed\\n- Every API call made\\n- Cost per action\\n- Agent decision reasoning\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1 (Milestone 0-1)**: Foundation\\n- \\u2705 Agent consolidation\\n- \\u2705 Drum corps cleanup\\n- [ ] Frequent commits (auto-commit tool)\\n- [ ] Branch-based development\\n- [ ] State persistence\\n\\n**Phase 2 (Milestone 2-3)**: Quality & Visibility\\n- [ ] Automated CI agent\\n- [ ] Cost tracking\\n- [ ] Performance metrics\\n- [ ] Code review agent\\n\\n**Phase 3 (Milestone 4+)**: Advanced Features\\n- [ ] Agent performance learning\\n- [ ] Multi-provider routing\\n- [ ] Web dashboard\\n- [ ] Agent composition engine\\n\\n**Phase 4 (Future)**: Innovation\\n- [ ] Self-healing agents\\n- [ ] Distributed execution\\n- [ ] Voice interface\\n- [ ] Advanced collaboration\\n\\n## Notes\\n- Features marked HIGH PRIORITY should be in next 2-3 milestones\\n- MEDIUM PRIORITY features can wait until system is stable\\n- ADVANCED features require significant R&D\\n- Get user feedback before implementing FUTURE features\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PqwXnQo36kK1xh3METxNuv', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'c7dc6764', 'category': 'decision', 'note': 'Analyzed FUTURE_FEATURES.md document - contains 22 major features/enhancements spanning development workflow, code quality, cost tracking, UX improvements, advanced agent features, and infrastructure. Document includes clear prioritization (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/ADVANCED) and phases. Will focus on implementing highest priority items first: frequent commits, branch-based development, CI agent, cost tracking, knowledge repository, and state persistence.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PqwXnQo36kK1xh3METxNuv', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VrHSYTts2hwMz4BnRE5nTe', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Future Features Implementation Requirements\n\n## Vision\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\n\n## Objectives\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\n\n## Scope\n\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\n\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\n\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\n\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\n\n## Target Users\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\n\n## Constraints\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\n\n## Technical Requirements\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\n- Mobile application interface\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\n- Frequent commits system\n- Branch-based development\n- State persistence\n- Secrets management\n\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \n- CI/CD agent\n- Cost tracking\n- Performance metrics\n- Code review automation\n\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\n- Knowledge repository agent\n- Agent performance learning\n- Multi-provider routing\n- Self-healing capabilities\n\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\n- Web dashboard\n- Integration capabilities\n- Advanced collaboration features\n\n## Assumptions Made\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\n\n## Dependencies\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VrHSYTts2hwMz4BnRE5nTe', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_231347.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_231347.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014ZGK2jXMtcn8yU32Xb91Jz', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'c7dc6764', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements documentation completed. Analyzed 22 features from FUTURE_FEATURES.md and created c