{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:18:17", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c98aef98-0de1-46d7-b451-e1a96e002622', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Future Features Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019U9ddEXzth6CSo3F5uwWCE', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019U9ddEXzth6CSo3F5uwWCE', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QrMgwxbrFPFQu7sc8f93hw', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': "# Future Features Implementation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nImplementing 22 advanced features for the Ensemble multi-agent development platform, focusing on workflow improvements, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience enhancements.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation Infrastructure (Weeks 1-3)\n**Objective**: Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Enhanced git commit system with agent attribution\n- Branch-based development workflow \n- State persistence and recovery mechanisms\n- Secrets management framework\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management  \n3. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\n4. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents automatically create meaningful commits with attribution\n- Branch creation/switching works seamlessly with agent coordination\n- System can recover from interruptions using checkpoints\n- All secrets are encrypted and accessed through secure vault\n- Zero regressions in existing functionality\n- Full test coverage for new git and persistence tools\n\n**Dependencies**: Existing git tooling, database persistence layer\n\n### Milestone 2: Quality Assurance & Monitoring (Weeks 4-6)\n**Objective**: Implement automated quality checks and comprehensive monitoring infrastructure\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Continuous integration agent for automated testing\n- Cost tracking and budgeting system\n- Performance metrics collection and dashboard\n- Automated code review capabilities\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n5. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\n6. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\n7. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\n8. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- CI agent runs comprehensive tests on all commits\n- Real-time cost tracking with configurable budget alerts\n- Performance dashboard shows agent success rates and efficiency metrics\n- Code review agent identifies quality issues before merge\n- All quality checks integrate with branch workflow\n- Cost tracking accuracy within 5% of actual usage\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (branch workflow), LLM provider APIs for cost data\n\n### Milestone 3: Intelligent Coordination (Weeks 7-9)\n**Objective**: Enable advanced agent coordination and knowledge management\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Knowledge repository for project context\n- Concurrent agent execution system\n- Agent collaboration protocols\n- Multi-provider LLM routing\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n9. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\n10. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\n11. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\n12. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Knowledge repository maintains comprehensive project context\n- Multiple agents can work on different branches simultaneously\n- Agents can communicate and coordinate across branches\n- LLM routing optimizes model selection based on task requirements\n- No conflicts between concurrent agent sessions\n- Knowledge base integrates with all agent decisions\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (branch system), Milestone 2 (monitoring infrastructure)\n\n### Milestone 4: Advanced Intelligence (Weeks 10-12)\n**Objective**: Implement self-optimizing and self-healing capabilities\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Agent performance learning system\n- Self-healing failure recovery\n- Comprehensive audit trail\n- Agent composition engine\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n13. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\n14. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\n15. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\n16. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- System learns from agent performance and optimizes future assignments\n- Automatic failure detection with strategy adjustment\n- Complete audit trail of all agent actions and decisions\n- Automated pipeline generation based on task complexity\n- Performance improvements measurable over baseline\n- Self-healing reduces manual intervention by 80%\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (performance metrics), Milestone 3 (agent coordination)\n\n### Milestone 5: User Experience & Integration (Weeks 13-15)\n**Objective**: Create interactive interfaces and external integrations\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Interactive web dashboard\n- Documentation generator agent\n- Slack/Discord integration\n- Docker-based execution environment\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n17. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\n18. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\n19. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\n20. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Web dashboard provides real-time visibility and control\n- Automated documentation generation for all projects\n- Slack/Discord integration supports common commands\n- Containerized execution improves isolation and reliability\n- Dashboard supports manual intervention during execution\n- Generated documentation meets quality standards\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (metrics dashboard), Milestone 4 (audit trail)\n\n### Milestone 6: Future Technologies (Weeks 16-18)\n**Objective**: Implement advanced distributed capabilities (Optional/Future)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Distributed agent execution system\n- Voice interface prototype\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents can execute across multiple machines\n- Voice interface supports basic project commands\n- Distributed execution maintains consistency\n- Voice interface integrates with dashboard\n\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones, additional infrastructure for distribution\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### High Risk Items\n- **Concurrent agent coordination**: Complex locking and conflict resolution\n- **State persistence reliability**: Critical for recovery scenarios\n- **Cost tracking accuracy**: Must be precise for budget management\n\n### Medium Risk Items  \n- **Performance impact of monitoring**: New features shouldn't slow system\n- **Security of secrets management**: Must follow enterprise security practices\n- **Integration complexity**: Multiple new systems interacting\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n- Comprehensive testing at each milestone\n- Rollback capabilities for all new features\n- Security review for credential handling\n- Performance benchmarking throughout implementation\n- Incremental feature activation with feature flags\n\n## Dependencies & Prerequisites\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture\n- Git repository and branch management\n- Database/persistence infrastructure  \n- LLM provider API access\n- Container runtime environment (for later milestones)\n- Web framework for dashboard development\n\n## Resource Requirements\n- Development team familiar with Ensemble architecture\n- Database administrator for persistence setup\n- Security engineer for secrets management review\n- DevOps engineer for CI/CD and containerization\n- UI/UX support for dashboard development\n\n## Success Metrics\n- All HIGH PRIORITY features (7 features) fully implemented\n- Zero regressions in existing functionality\n- Cost tracking within 5% accuracy\n- 80% reduction in manual intervention through self-healing\n- Performance improvements measurable in agent efficiency\n- Complete test coverage for all new features\n- User documentation for all implemented features\n\n## Communication Plan\n- Weekly milestone reviews\n- Daily standup for active development phases\n- Security and architecture reviews at milestone boundaries\n- Stakeholder demos at milestone completion\n- Risk assessment updates as needed"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_resul